on_at.sql, V2026.08.28__group_mention_at_rollback.sql, USE DB_YOPU_IM, INFORMATION_SCHEMA, DR\r\nOP IF EXISTS, TB_MESSAGE_MENTION, TB_GROUP_MENTION_IDEMPOTENCY, LAST_MENTION_MSG_ID, MENTIONS_JSON\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Re-test dev @ flow, 21/27 exposes 2006010 Snapshot V2 version split\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T10-04-09-rtMH-yopu_im_group_mention_all_rate_limit_nacos_permission_fix_ac.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\sprint\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\09\\01\\ro\r\nllout-2026-09-01T13-46-55-01a042ad-4e8f-73f0-92ff-21320d99f857_01a05b81-9b7b-7111-8259-403429bc8412.jsonl, updated_at=2\r\n026-09-01T06:24:16+00:00, thread_id=01a042ad-4e8f-73f0-92ff-21320d99f857, success: final 27/27 plus default 50/minute @\r\nall rate-limit verification)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 2006010, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader, buildV2GroupChatDecision, V2_ONLY, im.snapsh\r\not.auth.business-mode, policyVersion, memberVersion, FAIL_CLOSED, TB_IM_SNAPSHOT_DOMAIN_VERSION, GroupUserStatusFanoutS\r\nervice\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when requesting dev @ acceptance with “用…两个号…走sms-login…测试” -> exercise real accounts through the production-e\r\nquivalent login path and persist the runtime result in the formal acceptance document. [Task 1]\r\n- when asking “ddl有回滚脚本吗？sql脚本有use database吗” -> treat paired rollback and an explicit `USE <database>;` hea\r\nder as default DDL delivery checks; state their safety boundary. [Task 2]\r\n- when asking “测试下dev的@ 功能” -> reuse or reconstruct the acceptance script, then keep investigating a failure to d\r\nistinguish product behavior from environment-level data/runtime defects. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- WS contract verified here: cmd=1/2 login, 3/4 heartbeat, 11 group send, 12 ACK/push, 8 read, and 9/10 offline. The re\r\nal dual-client script covers login, heartbeat, ACK/@ echo, push, read, offline, authorization, idempotency, and symmetr\r\nic @all; results belong in `docs/architecture/群聊支持@功能-服务端实施测试验收方案-20260827.md`. [Task 1]\r\n- Normalize sms-login `data.userInfo.userId` with `int(...)`; on Windows make the script console-safe with `sys.stdout.\r\nreconfigure(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")`. Allow time after ACK before closing a receiver for offline assertions\r\n because MQ delivery can still be in flight. [Task 1]\r\n- Both forward and rollback scripts start with `USE DB_YOPU_IM;`. The forward migration covers mention tables and the l\r\nisted session/offline/pending columns; rollback uses INFORMATION_SCHEMA guards and `DROP ... IF EXISTS`, deletes struct\r\nure rather than backing up data, and therefore requires the feature off plus a data backup before execution. [Task 2]\r\n- Current dev failure signature: group send cmd=12 returns `2006010` when V2_ONLY reads a group whose policy and member\r\n manifests have divergent versions. Check group policy/recipients/member manifests in Redis plus `DB_YOPU_CRM.TB_IM_SNA\r\nPSHOT_DOMAIN_VERSION`; this was reproduced on a non-test group, so it is not a test-account exception. [Task 3]\r\n- The current reader strictly requires `policy.version == member.version`, while domain-local writes can increment memb\r\ner/recipients without policy; mismatch is only metered, and reconcile repairs missing rather than version-divergent dom\r\nains. Do not hand-edit code/data during diagnosis; choose and review either a coherent group-level version model or syn\r\nchronized write-side versioning. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: sms-login test reports an ID mismatch or crashes writing emoji. Cause: userId is a string and Windows consol\r\ne is GBK. Fix: normalize once with `int(...)` and configure UTF-8 replacement output. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: offline test wrongly treats an in-flight group push as a defect. Cause: a different MQ instance may consume \r\nthen route back after the client closes. Fix: add a delivery wait before close and use server log timing to classify th\r\ne race. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: `apply_patch` says `multiple operations target ...`. Fix: do Delete and Add for the same file in separate pa\r\ntches. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: any ordinary group send fails `2006010` before @ validation. Cause: V2 authorization cross-domain version mi\r\nsmatch under Mode C fail-closed. Fix: inspect Redis manifests and the domain-version table; do not mask it by weakening\r\n acceptance or changing shared dev data without a reviewed repair. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM Snapshot V2 warmup completeness, FRIEND_VIEW tombstone repair, cache versioning\r\n, and Outbox throughput\r\nscope: Prove dev Snapshot V2 warmup completeness with Redis SCAN versus DB authority, repair private-view tombstone exp\r\nosure, and route V1/V2 cache-version or cache-invalidation Outbox questions.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=branch=sprint3-0902-rrp and dev host\r\ns/configuration are time-sensitive; reuse the gates and diagnosis sequence, but recheck deployment, route, data, and Na\r\ncos state.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Dev IM Snapshot V2 warmup completeness scan and FRIEND_VIEW tombstone fix\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-27T07-20-48-6j2y-dev_im_snapshot_v2_warmup_completeness_scan_friendview_tombs.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\09\\01\\rollout-2\r\n026-09-01T14-20-21-01a04217-c167-7433-bd4a-fba8e0ad87aa_01a05ba0-3709-7711-a4ba-6ad50edbc6a5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-\r\n31T12:32:12+00:00, thread_id=01a04217-c167-7433-bd4a-fba8e0ad87aa, success: active-data completeness evidence, read-sid\r\ne tombstone fix, and runtime functional verification)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- ImSnapshotV2Keys, ImAuthCacheWarmupTask, ImPrivateViewSnapshotProjector, ImPhase4SnapshotReconcileTask, ProfileSnapsh\r\notV2Reader, FriendRelationServiceImpl, friendViewHash, decideFriendView, Redis SCAN, TB_FRIEND_RELATION, C1MissingPolic\r\nyMatrixTest, friend-view, TOMBSTONE\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Explain V1/V2 Redis cache versioning when adding a cache\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-28T08-26-53-TXGy-youpu_v2_cache_versioning_and_outbox_slow_consumption.md (cwd=D:\\workspace\r\n\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\09\\01\\rollout-2026-09-01T1\r\n4-27-09-01a0477a-9f93-7620-aba8-2a041f9eedb2_01a05ba6-6f2a-71b1-8598-4f31359add8e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T10:03:51\r\n+00:00, thread_id=01a0477a-9f93-7620-aba8-2a041f9eedb2, success: source-verified architecture Q&A; no code changes)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- RedisKeySpec, RedisKeyConstant, ImSnapshotV2Keys, ImSnapshotV2Payload, schemaVersion, versionDomain, BUSINESS_V1, WAR\r\nMUP_V1, hash tag, V1/V2, Redis-DataContract-V1-20260828.md, formal, staging, manifest, fence\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Diagnose cache-invalidation Outbox consumption capped at ~200/min\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-28T08-26-53-TXGy-youpu_v2_cache_versioning_and_outbox_slow_consumption.md (cwd=D:\\workspace\r\n\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\09\\01\\rollout-2026-09-01T1\r\n4-27-09-01a0477a-9f93-7620-aba8-2a041f9eedb2_01a05ba6-6f2a-71b1-8598-4f31359add8e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-28T10:03:51\r\n+00:00, thread_id=01a0477a-9f93-7620-aba8-2a041f9eedb2, success: source-verified throughput diagnosis; no configuration\r\n changed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- CacheInvalidationOutboxProcessor, CacheInvalidationOutboxStatusService, TB_RELATION_CACHE_INVALIDATION_OUTBOX, BATCH_\r\nSIZE, fixedDelay, tryClaim, lease, PENDING, PROCESSING, RETRYING, FAILED, outbox_pending_oldest_seconds, 200/min\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asks “通过测试了吗，预热数据都完整存在吗” -> do not make a verbal runtime claim; scan each Redis domain\r\n against DB authority and give the evidence table first. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user says “修复” after a concrete remaining defect is found -> complete the locate → patch → unit test → dep\r\nloyment/runtime-verification loop instead of only reporting it. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user says “部署dev了” -> autonomously verify the deployed JAR bytecode and exercise the business read before\r\n reporting acceptance; state honestly when a metric window cannot verify an immediate counter delta. [Task 1]\r\n- when asking “为什么这么慢” with changed backlog numbers (1577 PENDING; later repair batch 43877–44030 at ~200/min) ->\r\n read the actual constants, calculate items/minute, per-item path, and remaining time, then give actionable options; do\r\n not stop at “设计如此”. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- For a completeness run, derive each Redis SCAN pattern from the key builders, then compare active READY (`state=READY\r\n`, `versionDomain=BUSINESS_V1`, `version>0`) against DB authority: `TB_USER.STATUS=1 AND DELETED=0`, active groups, dis\r\ntinct friend-view owners, and non-deleted group-member owners. `TB_USER` primary key is `ID`, not `USER_ID`; `TB_FRIEND\r\n_RELATION` has no `DELETED` column. [Task 1]\r\n- Key-shape shield: member manifests use `yopu:im:auth:v2:group:{*}:member:*:manifest` because the member uid is not ha\r\nsh-tagged; `...:member:{*}:manifest` returns 0 falsely. Parse user/group ids with `strip('{}')`, not fixed `split(':')[\r\nn]` indexes. A 0 `member:index` is normal because it has no writer/reader beyond key construction and tests. [Task 1]\r\n- Dev evidence then showed active business coverage complete: profile 2877/2877, active group-member 1724/1724, friendV\r\niew owners 1452/1451 with one status=0 residual. uid=0 is intentionally excluded by the warmup cursor; deleted group TO\r\nMBSTONE manifests are formal state, not dirty data. [Task 1]\r\n- FRIEND_VIEW status=0 is a formal tombstone written/rebuilt by the normal delete path. `ProfileSnapshotV2Reader.decide\r\nFriendView` must filter non-1 status and return null without V1 fallback, matching group-member visibility; changing th\r\ne writer to HDEL would conflict with REPAIR/reconcile semantics. Validate `C1MissingPolicyMatrixTest` and the conversat\r\nion-record path for both deleted and normal friends. [Task 1]\r\n- Deployment proof uses `unzip -p` + `javap` on `ProfileSnapshotV2Reader.class`, then `/v1/im/conversation/records`: de\r\nleted friend `remark=null` while normal friend remarks remain. The `friend-view|C|tombstone` log is a per-minute/limite\r\nd aggregate, so its immediate increment is not a reliable P0 assertion. [Task 1]\r\n- V1/V2 is Key-namespace isolation: the `:v2:` segment, not a value's `version`, distinguishes a major cache generation\r\n. `schemaVersion` is payload/protocol shape (current `ImSnapshotV2Payload.SCHEMA_VERSION=1`); `versionDomain` is `WARMU\r\nP_V1` versus `BUSINESS_V1` data origin; `version` is same-object monotonic/CAS protection. Do not copy the stale `schem\r\naVersion: 2` example from `docs/yopu-cloud-platform-缓存架构整改方案-V1.0.md`. [Task 2]\r\n- V2 templates must retain Redis runtime hash tags: `{{userId}}`/`{{groupId}}` become `{arg}` in `ImSnapshotV2Keys`, wh\r\nereas V1 single-brace placeholders lose braces. Existing V1 upgrades use an independent `:v2:` Key plus dual write and \r\nShadow comparison; new caches can start directly at V2. Register each Key in `RedisKeySpec` with Type/Codec/Schema, and\r\n never mix `StringCodec` and `JsonJacksonCodec` on one Key. Snapshot V2 needs same-tag formal/staging/manifest/fence; o\r\nrdinary C2 caches do not need the full snapshot protocol. [Task 2]\r\n- For compatible additive payload changes, stay in the current key namespace and handle compatibility through `schemaVe\r\nrsion`; use `v2` → `v3` only for destructive changes. When retiring V1, explicitly clean the old namespace, manifest, a\r\nnd fence by domain to avoid `noeviction` capacity leakage. [Task 2]\r\n- Slow cache-invalidation Outbox consumption is intentional in this checkout: `CacheInvalidationOutboxProcessor` has `B\r\nATCH_SIZE=200`, `@Scheduled(fixedDelay=60_000)`, and oldest-first scanning, so 1577 PENDING needs at least eight cycles\r\n (about eight minutes plus work); ~8800 records need about 44 minutes under the same ceiling. Actual cycle time is proc\r\nessing plus the fixed 60-second delay. [Task 3]\r\n- Each item is serial `tryClaim` (`REQUIRES_NEW`) → MySQL fact read/Redis staging+formal/Lua RENAME/manifest/fence-CAS \r\nprojection → `markCompleted` (`REQUIRES_NEW`), so DB/Redis round trips dominate. PENDING disappearing after claim means\r\n PROCESSING, not completed; retries use `min(60*2^N,3600)` and future `NEXT_RETRY_TIME` records are not scanned. `LEASE\r\n_DURATION_SECONDS=120`; acceptance remains `outbox_pending_oldest_seconds<120s` and `FAILED=0`. Safe semantic-preservin\r\ng accelerators are larger batch, shorter delay, or more instances because `tryClaim` atomically prevents duplicate owne\r\nrship. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: a SCAN pattern returns 0 although the code writes the domain. Cause: the key pattern or hash-tag placement i\r\ns wrong. Fix: first broad-scan (`group:*:member*`) and inspect the real key shape; do not report missing warmup data un\r\ntil the pattern is proven. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: a private-view tombstone looks like a delete-path cleanup defect. Cause: the write/reconcile contract delibe\r\nrately retains status=0. Fix: inspect the writer and reconciliation semantics before changing data; repair the reader-s\r\nide visibility filter. [Task 1]\r\n- PowerShell has no heredoc (`python - <<'PY'` causes `ParserError`). Write a temporary `.py` with `apply_patch`, then \r\nexecute it. `rg -n -S \"...{{userId}}...\"` treats `{{` as regex; for literal templates use `Select-String -Path <files> \r\n-Pattern 'pat1','pat2'`. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / Redis Key domain inventory, task-board visualization, and IM-Account architecture \r\ndocumentation\r\nscope: Build source-backed Redis Key inventories using the required business-semantics/Type/Codec/Schema format; review\r\n against the codec contract, and deliver a visible all-domain board while preserving the source-vs-runtime boundary.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=key call sites and current checkout \r\ncoverage are branch-specific; the inventory method, codec roots, visualization pattern, and runtime-SCAN boundary are r\r\neusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Inventory, review, and correct all Redis Key domains\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T03-22-18-las0-yopu_redis_key_domain_inventory_and_visualization_review_fix.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\25\\rollo\r\nut-2026-08-25T11-22-18-01a036f0-b142-7fc3-89a4-884e2c566e68.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T02:41:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0\r\n36f0-b142-7fc3-89a4-884e2c566e68, success: 8-domain inventory and review fixes; source-only, no runtime Redis SCAN)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- RedisKeySpec.java, RedisKeyConstant.java, RedisKeyBuilder.java, RedisConfig.java, 业务语义, Redis Type, Codec, Schema\r\n, JsonJacksonCodec, StringCodec.INSTANCE, RedisTemplate, StringRedisTemplate, JetCache, ack:pending, deliver:*, conv:la\r\nst\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Archive the inventory and task-board tree in `docs/architecture/`\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T03-22-18-las0-yopu_redis_key_domain_inventory_and_visualization_review_fix.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\25\\rollo\r\nut-2026-08-25T11-22-18-01a036f0-b142-7fc3-89a4-884e2c566e68.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T02:41:17+00:00, thread_id=01a0\r\n36f0-b142-7fc3-89a4-884e2c566e68, success: two Markdown inventories plus previewable task-board HTML)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Redis-Key-域清单-20260825.md, Redis-Key-IM与Account域清单-20260825.md, Redis-Key-域结构树-20260826.html, docs/archite\r\ncture, task board, visualize, render.py, git status --short, Measure-Object -Line\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when requesting a Key inventory, the user specified: \"每个 Key 域固定按这个给我：业务语义 + Redis Type + Codec + Sche\r\nma\" -> group the result by domain and use exactly those four columns; state whether evidence is checkout source or a ru\r\nntime Redis scan. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user said \"落成md，同时IM和ACCOUNT单独给我罗列一个md\" -> archive important inventory results as Markdown and\r\n provide a focused IM+Account companion document. [Task 2]\r\n- when the user said \"我想一眼就能看到所有的分类，按任务面板的那种\" -> make category-overview visualizations previewabl\r\ne and fully expanded as parallel task-board panels in the project `docs/architecture/`, rather than a collapsible tree.\r\n [Task 2]\r\n- when the user replied only \"评审\" then \"修复\" -> first cross-check documentation against source facts and enumerate o\r\nutdated/contradictory/missing claims, then make the corresponding corrections. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Treat `yopu-common/.../redis/RedisKeySpec.java` as the key-codec authority: `RAW` means explicit `StringCodec` for cr\r\noss-service authorization/profile/private-view keys; `JSON` means the default `JsonJacksonCodec` for business cache. `R\r\nedisKeyConstant`/Builder define or construct keys but do not prove a call site. [Task 1]\r\n- `RedisConfig.java` establishes three serialization paths plus JetCache: Redisson defaults to `JsonJacksonCodec` (sing\r\nle-server forces pool 512/min idle 10), `RedisTemplate<String,Object>` uses `Jackson2JsonRedisSerializer` with default \r\ntyping, `StringRedisTemplate` is raw strings, and JetCache uses Java serialization. [Task 1]\r\n- `yopu:im:ack:pending:{toUserId}:{msgId}` was corrected on 2026-08-25 to use default JSON for both single and batch pa\r\nths; the prior `StringCodec`/JSON mixing caused `InvalidTypeIdException: missing type id property '@class'`. Do not ret\r\nain the obsolete “待收敛” conclusion. [Task 1]\r\n- Include the `trade-deliver` `deliver:*` domain: it has 13 prefixes and injects `RedisTemplate<String,String>` resolve\r\nd to the common Jackson2Json bean. `conv:last` has scoped and unscoped templates. Constants with no present call site r\r\nemain source-inferred and need per-environment SCAN before cleanup or runtime claims. [Task 1]\r\n- Current deliverables are `Redis-Key-域清单-20260825.md` (8 domains), `Redis-Key-IM与Account域清单-20260825.md`, and `\r\nRedis-Key-域结构树-20260826.html`. Use `git status --short`, line counts, targeted `rg`, and HTML/JS checks to verify d\r\nocument delivery. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: an inline visualization does not preview. Cause: the required rendering delimiter/format is missing. Fix: us\r\ne the complete `visualize{\"path\":\"<absolute-path>\"}` form and verify it in-session before calling it delivered. [Task 2\r\n]\r\n- In PowerShell, `head` is unavailable; use `Select-Object -First`. Quote `rg` regexes with single quotes, avoid wildca\r\nrd-like filenames as an `rg` file argument, and obtain exact Chinese/escaped patch context with `rg -n` before `apply_p\r\natch`. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / Douyin data-acceptance report refresh and traffic analysis\r\nscope: Update `reports/数据验收报告.md` from the user's logged-in Chrome session or user-provided platform screenshots;\r\n keep account-level and per-work metrics, source boundaries, and traffic analysis evidence-bounded.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat; reuse_rule=browser-control paths and platform metric\r\ns 