unnel_audit_village_data_refre.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\25\\rollout-20\r\n26-08-25T21-59-31-01a03938-1522-7350-a730-c127f24f7288.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T01:33:59+00:00, thread_id=01a03938-\r\n1522-7350-a730-c127f24f7288, partial: official-source audit completed; scoring redesign proposed, not adopted; live rep\r\nort refresh succeeded)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 抖音算法, 推流漏斗, 平均阅读深度占比, 完读率, 划走率, Spearman, 本地分vs平台实绩, trust.douyin.com, reports/数据验收\r\n报告.md, 回村中巴捡MP4, 村子, A档强势早期, 4:5, 9:16\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asks “更新最新的数据验收报告，粉丝数量、等，然后分析流量” and corrects “粉丝数量是54了” -> live-recolle\r\nct account inventory and per-work indicators in the logged-in Creator Center before analysis; a screenshot/hand-entered\r\n count is a cue to recollect, not a replacement for the current platform snapshot. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user pastes an external algorithm explanation with no source links and asks “和我项目对比” -> audit it again\r\nst project standards and real platform data, verify it against official sources, and distinguish “officially confirmed \r\n/ not public / operating inference”; do not rename project scores or treat reposted claims as fact. [Task 3]\r\n- the user repeatedly used bare “继续” -> advance to the next concrete analysis/recollection/report-update step without\r\n requiring step-by-step prompting, while retaining the repo/platform evidence boundary. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Read `START_HERE.md` and `SKILL.md` before report edits; `<episode>/meta/episode-state.json` is the machine-state sou\r\nrce and document authority is `制作规范_正式版 > active subordinate > series overlay > reference > superseded`. [Task 1\r\n][Task 2]\r\n- `reports/数据验收报告.md` is the account-data authority. Its fixed sections are conclusion, evidence boundary, accoun\r\nt overview, published-work table, priority-work funnel diagnosis, traffic/release decision, and collection backlog. `当\r\n前总览` must not impersonate official 6h/24h/48h/7d cards; never backfill a missed formal checkpoint from a later overv\r\niew. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- Related skill: skills/douyin-creator-center-report/SKILL.md. [Task 1]\r\n- Claim the logged-in tab titled `抖音创作者中心`. Homepage supplies account inventory; Data Center cards supply rollin\r\ng seven-day metrics; `https://creator.douyin.com/creator-micro/content/manage` supplies per-work plays/likes/comments/f\r\navorites/shares/follows/均浏览图/划走率/文案展开率. Label distinct timestamps, do not split rolling seven-day totals in\r\nto one work, and treat small page differences as refresh lag rather than forcing reconciliation. [Task 1]\r\n- Platform publication is a platform fact. 《瓶中世界》 and 《鳌太线·热汤》 were platform-published while their repo st\r\nate remained `PUBLISH_READY` (the latter also lacks `publish-event.json`); record that discrepancy, then use V2.1 `post\r\n_publish_review.py mark-published` as a separate formal transition. Never hand-edit `current_state` or fabricate a publ\r\nish event. [Task 2]\r\n- Recount rows and sums (播放/评论/吸粉), run `git diff --check`, and grep superseded values after every report edit; t\r\nhis 08-31 refresh also used `rg -c '^\\\\| (\\\\*\\\\*)?([0-9]+)'` to confirm 22 work rows. [Task 2]\r\n- Use the four-layer reading: L1 entry (`划走率`) → L2 reading carry (`均浏览图`/average reading depth) → L3 interactio\r\nn (likes/comments/favorites/shares) → L4 follows; rates use the play denominator. `均浏览图 ÷ 总张数` is average readin\r\ng-depth share, not completion rate/末页到达率. [Task 2][Task 3]\r\n- Before editing a high-churn report, reread current exact lines with `rg`/`Get-Content`; after edits run `git diff --c\r\nheck -- 'reports/数据验收报告.md'` and grep superseded values throughout the report. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- Four-layer diagnostic: L1 entry (`划走率`) → L2 reading carry (`均浏览图`) → L3 interaction (likes/comments/favorites\r\n/shares) → L4 follows. At the 08-31 snapshot, 《瓶中世界》 was ~51h and “基本进入长尾” (strong L1/L2, weak L3/L4); 《鳌\r\n太线·热汤》 was ~23.5h (comments signal, 0 follows) and still needs a 48h read. Treat these as operating inference, not\r\n an official algorithm claim. [Task 1]\r\n- For the 17-work account sample, plays correlate with 均浏览图 (Spearman about +0.76) and 平均阅读深度占比 (about +0.6\r\n1), and inversely with 划走率 (about -0.76); this supports “先停留、再深读” for this account but is correlation, not pl\r\natform-weight causality. Official Douyin material supports user-content matching, multi-round ranking, and behavior-pro\r\nbability prediction, not fixed traffic-pool tiers or percentage weights. [Task 3]\r\n- Keep local pre-publication/production acceptance scores separate from post-publication recommendation performance. 《\r\n村子》 at the 2026-08-26 refresh was 474 plays, 均浏览 9.6, 划走率 27.85%, average depth 45.7%, and only “A档强势早期”;\r\n do not redo title/cover/front sequence solely on this point or let one 4:5 result override the 9:16 gate. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: `apply_patch verification failed: Failed to find expected lines`. Cause: the report has frequently changed a\r\nnd the patch used stale context. Fix: read current UTF-8 lines with `rg`/`Get-Content` before patching; if a page snaps\r\nhot is older than the report, retain the newer report snapshot rather than overwriting it. [Task 1]\r\n- A dynamic Creator Center/public-homepage timeout means missing evidence, not “no new post.” Account-level fans/likes \r\nmust be live-recollected or explicitly labelled as a prior verified snapshot; never present them as current. Never back\r\nfill a missed 6h/24h/48h/7d checkpoint from a later overview. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / first audio-video call after friend addition has no callee response\r\nscope: Diagnose intermittent first-call signal loss with static code/git evidence; route future investigations to runti\r\nme call/routing logs before implementing a fix.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=class lines, branch state, commits, \r\nand dev endpoints are checkout/time-specific; signal-chain tracing and evidence thresholds are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Diagnose first voice/video call ignored, second or third call works\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-22T07-59-31-LoVE-yopu_im_first_call_after_friend_add_no_response_analysis.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wo\r\nrkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\22\\rollout-2\r\n026-08-22T15-59-31-01a0287b-6739-7712-8186-ef0a884e9b7e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-22T08:30:43+00:00, thread_id=01a0287b\r\n-6739-7712-8186-ef0a884e9b7e, uncertain: static chain verified; no runtime [CALL_DEBUG] evidence)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- CallServiceImpl, initiateCall, sendCallSignal, CALL_INVITE, CALL_DEBUG, getUserRoutes, route:user:clients, SIGNAL_EXC\r\nHANGE, consumeSignal, 音视频信令投递失败，用户不在线, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, b001ea6ac\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- for an IM symptom report, the user twice replied only “继续” during investigation -> continue the read-only chain (me\r\nmory → code → git history → executable evidence plan) rather than stopping early for speculation or unnecessary clarifi\r\ncation. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Call chain is `IMHandler.handleCallInvite` → `IMServiceImpl.initiateCall` → `CallServiceImpl.initiateCall` → `sendCal\r\nlSignal(calleeId, CALL_INVITE)`. It is synchronous on the Netty worker and does not pass `authorizeSingleChat` / `Relat\r\nionAuthorizationSnapshotReader`; `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`, friend-snapshot fence, and welcome-message conclusions do\r\n not explain call delivery. [Task 1]\r\n- `sendCallSignal` chooses local `channelManager.sendToUser`, remote `MessageProducer.sendSignal` to `SIGNAL_EXCHANGE` \r\nwith `{serverId}.signal`, then direct fallback when `hasActiveChannel`. `MessageConsumer.consumeSignal` ACK-drops a rem\r\note signal if the callee has no active channel: “信令无重试队列/DLQ，直接丢弃并告警.” [Task 1]\r\n- Route model is per-client `yopu:im:route:user:{userId}:{clientType}` plus client set `yopu:im:route:user:clients:{use\r\nrId}` and legacy single key; online means `onlineStatus==1`, TTL 180s. On this checkout `CALL_DEBUG=true`; inspect `rou\r\nteCount`, decision/fallback lines, the offline warning, and client CALL_INVITE/UI evidence before ranking root causes. \r\n`routeCount=0` while online points first to a missing clients-set write. [Task 1]\r\n- Historical route leads: `b001ea6ac` covers non-atomic RBatch route writes/client-set loss; `86de7f055` covers RBatch \r\nread contention via getAsync+30s cache. The candidate retry/refresh/client UI remedies remain proposals until runtime e\r\nvidence selects one. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not analogize call behavior from single-chat authorization snapshots before tracing the actual call path; the init\r\nial AUTH_SNAPSHOT hypothesis was disproved. [Task 1]\r\n- In PowerShell, `find` can return `Parameter format not correct` and formatted `Select-Object FullName` can truncate p\r\naths. Use `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter 'Name.java' | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }` or an exact full path. Probe de\r\nv endpoints with bounded parallel short timeouts after confirming connectivity. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: dashi-taskboard (Codex Taskboard) evaluation, local install, and Windows integration\r\nscope: Evaluate, install, and diagnose the local Codex Taskboard; distinguish its own task database from existing Codex\r\n tasks and keep the Windows service loopback-only.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=repository stars, release activity, package versions, defaults, an\r\nd CI state are time-sensitive; the evaluation workflow and local-network security checks are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Evaluate and locally install chuspeeism/dashi-taskboard\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- dashi-taskboard, chuspeeism/dashi-taskboard, Codex Taskboard, React 19, Node 22, SQLite, Tauri, taskctl, npm ci, npm \r\nrun check, /health, CODEX_TASKBOARD_HOST, 0.0.0.0:47823, 127.0.0.1, CDP, CSP, Windows unsigned\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user writes “dashi-taskboard 看看这个github仓库” without criteria -> respond in Chinese and proactively use \r\na structured repository assessment (identify → README/metadata/direct files → maturity/activity/risk → actionable trial\r\n recommendation), not a one-paragraph summary. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user says “看不到我codex正在执行的任务啊” -> explain that the browser version tracks only tasks created in i\r\nts own database; it does not import existing Codex tasks, and tracking starts from Taskboard. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Prefer the direct GitHub repository page and raw `README`/`package.json`/`AGENTS.md`/`LICENSE`/`PRIVACY.md` plus CI a\r\nnd commits over stale search snippets; search-result star counts diverged during this review. [Task 1]\r\n- The captured project was a local-first React 19 + Node 22 + SQLite + Tauri taskboard with `taskctl` and an internal C\r\nodex Skill using the same HTTP API. Default host `0.0.0.0:47823` has no LAN account authentication; for a local trial e\r\nxplicitly set `$env:CODEX_TASKBOARD_HOST = '127.0.0.1'`. Install at `D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\dashi-taskboar\r\nd` with `npm ci` then `npm run check`; verified health endpoint is `/health`, not `/api/health`. [Task 1]\r\n- The independent browser service cannot scan/import arbitrary existing Codex chats. For tracked work use Taskboard cre\r\nate task → “open in conversation” → Codex processes it → `taskctl` records `CODEX_THREAD_ID`. [Task 1]\r\n- On Windows/MS Store Codex, the source Launcher failed `Unable to inspect the launched Codex process`; prefer the offi\r\ncial NSIS installer if the user explicitly confirms its unsigned installer. Verify a resumed download's SHA-256 before \r\nopening it. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: search results disagree on repository statistics. Fix: cite/decide from the current direct repository page a\r\nnd raw files, not cached search cards. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Windows Codex C-drive space cleanup, generated-image junction, and session-growth diagnosis\r\nscope: Free C-drive capacity safely when Codex data or caches grow; use for repeated “C盘没空间了/又快满了” reports, wi\r\nth explicit boundaries around active sessions and live log storage.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=the machine paths, sizes, and free-space figures are local snapsho\r\nts; the C-drive triage order, D-drive image junction, and deletion safeguards are reusable on this machine.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: C盘满 – move generated images to D:\\codex-img and delete archived sessions\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-15T08-36-48-OgLK-windows_c_drive_codex_cleanup_image_migration_to_d.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79\r\n873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\15\\rollout-2026-08-15T16-36-48-01a00491-0510-7b8\r\n3-a246-9dec885909e0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T03:07:52+00:00, thread_id=01a00491-0510-7b83-a246-9dec885909e0, succes\r\ns: generated_images migrated as a Junction; archived sessions deleted and verified)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- C盘满, C盘又快满了, C drive full, Codex sessions, archived_sessions, generated_images, D:\\codex-img, Junction, logs_2\r\n.sqlite, npm-cache, Remove-Item blocked by policy, cmd /c rd /s /q, Get-Volume\r\n\r\n## Task 2: C盘又快满了 – identify active-session growth and remove new archived sessions\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-15T08-36-48-OgLK-windows_c_drive_codex_cleanup_image_migration_to_d.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79\r\n873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\15\\rollout-2026-08-15T16-36-48-01a00491-0510-7b8\r\n3-a246-9dec885909e0.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T03:07:52+00:00, thread_id=01a00491-0510-7b83-a246-9dec885909e0, partia\r\nl: growth source identified; follow-up active-session/cache cleanup still needs user selection)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- sessions 7GB, archived_sessions 176MB, generated_images LinkType Junction, D:\\codex-img, logs_2.sqlite, empty pipe el\r\nement, $rows=@(), cmd /c del /q, cmd /c rd /s /q\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user says “已归档任务记录，归档仍占硬盘 这些删除了；生成的图片，迁移到D盘，以后生产的图片也挪到D盘根目录下 c\r\nodex-img” -> treat `archived_sessions` as permanently deletable for this machine and keep generated images at `D:\\codex\r\n-img`; do not move them back to C. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user repeatedly reports “C盘没空间了” / “C盘又快满了” -> proactively use the established C-drive triage rath\r\ner than ask them to restate the situation. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- in a cleanup inventory, the user named only `archived_sessions` and `generated_images` -> do not also clear active `s\r\nessions`, config/auth/plugins, caches, or `logs_2.sqlite` without a separately scoped choice; numbered options are a lo\r\nw-friction way to obtain that choice. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Related skill: skills/windows-codex-storage-cleanup/SKILL.md. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- On this machine, C is a 200GB Windows SSD and the user experiences “full” at about 15–20GB free. First run `Get-Volum\r\ne`, then size `.codex` top-level directories; a junctioned `generated_images` reports content but does not consume C-dr\r\nive storage—confirm `Get-Item` `LinkType=Junction` and `Target=D:\\codex-img` before treating it as a cleanup candidate.\r\n [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\generated_images` is already a Junction to `D:\\codex-img`, so future Codex image output goes t\r\no D. A safe migration sequence is: check D free space -> `Move-Item` content -> verify source empty and target counts/s\r\nizes -> remove the source directory -> create `New-Item -ItemType Junction`; stop if source is not empty. [Task 1]\r\n- For repeated growth, inspect `.codex\\sessions` early: active JSONL files (some >1GB) grew from about 4.7GB to 7GB and\r\n explained the next C-drive drop. `archived_sessions` can be removed, but old active sessions and caches should be prop\r\nosed separately. [Task 2]\r\n- `logs_2.sqlite` is a large but live Codex database: do not delete or rebuild it while Codex is running. Consider its \r\nmaintenance only after a complete application exit. [Task 1]\r\n- For directory-size tabulation, collect objects into `$rows=@()` and then pipe `$rows | Format-Table -AutoSize`; a dir\r\nect `foreach {...} | Format-Table` can produce `An empty pipe element is not allowed`. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: a multi-line, quoted PowerShell command supplied to `exec_command` is rejected as `blocked by policy` before\r\n execution. Cause: local CreateProcess/argument parsing. Fix: write a temporary `.ps1` with `apply_patch`, execute `pow\r\nershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File '<path>'`, then remove the script; keep migration validation insid\r\ne the script. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: the local Codex runtime rejects `Remove-Item` as `blocked by policy`, even for a test file. Fix: resolve and\r\n verify the exact target first, then use `cmd /c del /q \"<file>\"` for files or `cmd /c rd /s /q \"<directory>\"` for expl\r\nicitly authorized directories; test this route on a temporary file before a real deletion. [Task 2]\r\n- Symptom: a root-wide recursive C-drive scan is slow and not actionable. Fix: target known large areas—`.codex`, user \r\ncaches, `ProgramData`, Temp, JetBrains—then drill down only into the top contributor. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / Android local joint-debug gateway routing and APK endpoint analysis\r\nscope: Connect a Yopu Android client to selected locally run services without disrupting the shared development environ\r\nment; use for local gateway path overrides, APK endpoint discovery, and environment-switch/repack decisions.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=repo routes and installed APK string\r\ns are checkout/package-specific; the shared-environment isolation and static-URL analysis procedure are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Route only selected Android service requests to locally run services\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T07-43-03-JYO6-yopu_android_local_debug_proxy_appconfig_env_analysis.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026\r\n-08-20T15-43-03-01a01e1f-9da5-77d2-a3a4-b7acfe4e48aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T02:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a01e1f-9d\r\na5-77d2-a3a4-b7acfe4e48aa, partial: design delivered; not yet implemented/verified on device)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 友圃, Yopu, 本地联调, 安卓包, yopu-gateway-core, 9001, Nacos, 10.168.1.233:9000, register-enabled=false, Path=/vX, St\r\nripPrefix, http://127.0.0.1:9221\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Change or inspect a built Android package for endpoint routing\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T07-43-03-JYO6-yopu_android_local_debug_proxy_appconfig_env_analysis.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026\r\n-08-20T15-43-03-01a01e1f-9da5-77d2-a3a4-b7acfe4e48aa.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T02:05:44+00:00, thread_id=01a01e1f-9d\r\na5-77d2-a3a4-b7acfe4e48aa, success: debug and beta endpoint behavior located)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- APK, localDebug, BuildConfig.BASE_URL, ApiConstants, RetrofitManager, ImWebSocketClient, AppConfig, classes20.dex, cl\r\nasses2.dex, 10.168.1.233:9001, api.youpuzg.com, androguard, const-string, usesCleartextTraffic\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user says “目前服务太多了，我本地电脑不可能全部部署……能不能本地启动，将安卓包的某几个服务的请求代理转到我本\r\n地服务” -> prioritize the smallest operational path that does not change or destabilize the shared development environm\r\nent. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asks “我能不能改他打好的包呢” or wants to switch a test package to development -> give a concrete cost-\r\nordered route: an existing debug/local build first, then source `localDebug`, then proxy/Frida, with APK repacking as l\r\nast-resort fallback. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- `yopu-gateway-core` defaults to port 9001 and uses static `Path=/vX/...` -> `lb://service` routes. Run the changed se\r\nrvice plus a local gateway; point the Android Debug package to local gateway `:9001`; override only required paths (for\r\n example `/v1/trade/order/** -> http://127.0.0.1:9221`) and let all other paths resolve through development Nacos. IM i\r\ns exceptional: `StripPrefix=1`; most other routes use `StripPrefix=0`. [Task 1]\r\n- Start both the local service and local gateway with `-Dspring.cloud.nacos.discovery.register-enabled=false`. This avo\r\nids same-name registration in shared Nacos and random traffic reaching the developer machine; stopping local processes \r\nthen cleanly falls back without a shared gateway change. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not direct the phone to a local business service (bypasses gateway JWT / `X-User-Id` injection), register the loca\r\nl instance in shared Nacos, or alter the shared gateway to point at a personal machine. Development data and async/MQ c\r\nallbacks can still interact with remote services, so verify phone authentication, local-hit logs, uncovered remote endp\r\noints, and no shared-environment impact after shutdown. [Task 1]\r\n- The preferred durable solution is Android source with a `localDebug` flavor that changes `BuildConfig.BASE_URL` / `Ap\r\niConstants` / Retrofit creation. An APK-only route requires decode -> locate domain -> edit -> rebuild -> zipalign -> s\r\nign; re-signing cannot replace the original formal app and signature/anti-tamper, channel verification, hot update, log\r\nin, push, or payment dependencies may fail. [Task 2]\r\n- In unpacked debug v2.10.6, `classes20.dex` `com/youpu/app/config/AppConfig` contains business gateway `http://10.168.\r\n1.233:9001/` and WebSocket `ws://10.168.1.233:9001/ws`; the `classes28.dex` `http://10.38.162.35:9085` belongs to an an\r\nalytics/logging SDK, not the business gateway. Search efficiently with `rg -a -o --no-filename \"10\\\\.168\\\\.\\\\d{1,3}\\\\.\\\r\n\\d{1,3}\" <dir> | Sort-Object -Unique`, then inspect surrounding strings/classes. [Task 2]\r\n- Beta v2.10.7 is not runtime-switchable: `RetrofitManager$retrofit$2;->invoke` hardcodes `https://api.youpuzg.com/` an\r\nd `ImWebSocketClient` hardcodes `wss://api.youpuzg.com/ws/`; apparent DEBUG/RELEASE/BETA enum code is overridden by `co\r\nnst-string`. Fastest route is the existing v2.10.6 debug package; HTTPS domain rewriting requires a trusted MITM certif\r\nicate and an on-device pinning check. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not assume a named `AppConfig` class survives in a beta/release APK: v2.10.7 was obfuscated. When `rg` class-name \r\nsearch fails, locate URLs by scanning each DEX method's `const-string`/`const-string/jumbo` instructions and infer owne\r\nrship from the containing class/method. [Task 2]\r\n- Symptom: `baksmali` URL returns 404 or local `jadx`/`apktool` is unavailable. Fix: install/use `androguard` (`python \r\n-m pip install androguard`); silence its logs with `logging.getLogger('androguard').setLevel(logging.CRITICAL)`. New `g\r\net_strings_analysis()` returns a dict, and xrefs may be incomplete, so direct bytecode scanning is more reliable. [Task\r\n 2]\r\n- Symptom: parallel analysis commands report `file used by another process`. Cause: shared stderr/log target. Fix: give\r\n each command a distinct log file. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM Redis snapshot Phase 2-4 authorization, dev acceptance, and contracts\r\nscope: Review and validate the one-domain-one-snapshot migration for IM user/group authorization, manifests, fences, Ou\r\ntbox, SHADOW cutover, Phase 3 dev dual writes, and Phase 4 contracts; product code/deployment remains separately author\r\nized.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=source locations, current branches, \r\ndev/PRD topology, and rollout state are checkout/time-specific; codec consistency and fail-closed migration invariants \r\nare reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Inventory IM Redis snapshot omissions, codec boundaries, and Phase 0-5 compatibility\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-21T06-05-17-y5zE-im_redis_snapshot_refactor_omission_inventory.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQ\r\nianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\26\\rollout-2026-08-26T1\r\n1-29-01-01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126_01a03c1d-30d1-7be3-979a-0958cee40032.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T05:39:09\r\n+00:00, thread_id=01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126, success: omission inventory and architecture document added; co\r\nmpatibility/checkpoint answers are explanatory, not run validation)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IM-Redis快照改造遗漏盘点-20260826.md, JsonJacksonCodec, StringCodec, InvalidTypeIdException, GROUP_STATS, FRIEND_VIEW\r\n, GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW, JetCache, deliver:*, RedisTemplate, SHADOW, legacy-write\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Phase 3 B6 dev group-four-domain V2 dual-write acceptance retest\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T10-46-51-ED4o-youpu_im_snapshot_phase3_dev_acceptance_and_phase4_contract.md (cwd=D:\\wor\r\nkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\27\\rollout-2026-0\r\n8-27T15-22-49-01a03887-aefc-71e1-9214-855123ce83ec_01a04219-9bc3-77e1-bd89-72092125e57e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T16\r\n:28:56+00:00, thread_id=01a03887-aefc-71e1-9214-855123ce83ec, success: 11-step dev acceptance passed; no product-code c\r\nhange)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- tmp_phase3_dev_accept.py, GROUP_POLICY, GROUP_RECIPIENTS, GROUP_MEMBER, GROUP_REVIEW, ImGroupSnapshotV2Projector, ImG\r\nroupSnapshotV2Keys, allowMemberMute, 1004019, 1015003, TB_RELATION_CACHE_INVALIDATION_OUTBOX, manifest READY, legacy sn\r\napshot\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Phase 4 contract static review for seven profile/group/view domains\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-25T10-46-51-ED4o-youpu_im_snapshot_phase3_dev_acceptance_and_phase4_contract.md (cwd=D:\\wor\r\nkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\27\\rollout-2026-0\r\n8-27T15-22-49-01a03887-aefc-71e1-9214-855123ce83ec_01a04219-9bc3-77e1-bd89-72092125e57e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T16\r\n:28:56+00:00, thread_id=01a03887-aefc-71e1-9214-855123ce83ec, success: contract v0.3 passed static review; coding/deplo\r\nyment not authorized)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IM-Redis快照Phase4实现契约-20260827.md, PROFILE_SUMMARY, PROFILE_FULL, PROFILE_STATS, GROUP_PROFILE, GROUP_STATS, FRI\r\nEND_VIEW, GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW, SHA256_CANONICAL_JSON_V1, safety fence, *_V2, ConversationServiceImpl, joinTime fail-close\r\nd\r\n\r\n## Task 4: Define when dual writes are compatible and when to check alignment\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-21T06-05-17-y5zE-im_redis_snapshot_refactor_omission_inventory.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQ\r\nianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\26\\rollout-2026-08-26T1\r\n1-29-01-01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126_01a03c1d-30d1-7be3-979a-0958cee40032.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-26T05:39:09\r\n+00:00, thread_id=01a022ec-756e-7550-8c81-f92d7843c126, success: staged compatibility explanation; the proposed checkli\r\nst was not separately adopted)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Phase 0-5, dual-write, SHADOW, domain-read, legacy-write, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, COMPLETED, PENDING, RETRYING, FA\r\nILED, manifest READY, mismatch, REPAIR Outbox\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked “给我一个新的 md” -> Redis/IM analysis documents in this repo should use the existing `主题-YYYYM\r\nMDD` naming and `docs/architecture/` placement. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asked “每一步实施完都能兼容旧的缓存吗” -> state the mechanism and the “断旧” boundary per phase, not a \r\nblanket “能”. [Task 3]\r\n- when the user asked “什么时候需要检查下是否双写全部成功，同时对齐” -> provide a “何时/查什么/通过标准” cutover checkl\r\nist. [Task 3]\r\n- when the user says “dev部署了，重新测试” -> first verify the deployed JAR/process is the intended fix, wait for RETRY\r\nING Outbox convergence, then run the complete acceptance chain rather than only rerunning assertions. [Task 2]\r\n- when the user asks “评审，如果不通过则补强继续评审” -> use a formal blocking-item loop and state a clear pass/fail ou\r\ntcome; do not leave unresolved correctness or privacy gaps under a nominally reviewable contract. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- One Redis key must use one codec: use `StringCodec` for authorization/profile snapshots, private views, fence/ready, \r\nand Lua state; the `RedisConfig` default `JsonJacksonCodec` is for DTO/Map/object caches. The historical `yopu:im:ack:p\r\nending` single/batch/retry mix caused `InvalidTypeIdException: missing type id property '@class'` and was unified on 20\r\n26-08-25. [Task 1]\r\n- Phase 0-5 cover 11 of 14 snapshot domains; `GROUP_STATS`, `FRIEND_VIEW`, and `GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW` remain unplanned. Je\r\ntCache's Java `value-encoder` is a separate modernization line, and `deliver:*` serialization must be confirmed by envi\r\nronment scan because its declared `RedisTemplate<String,String>` conflicts with the injected Jackson-valued bean. [Task\r\n 1]\r\n- The Phase 3 11-step dev test validates formal+manifest version rows, fences, Outbox `COMPLETED`, and legacy group wri\r\ntes across create→join→admin→member mute→mute-all→review→kick→leave→dissolve. V2 keys use real `{gid}` hash tags; legac\r\ny `yopu:im:auth:group:%d:snapshot` has no braces. [Task 2]\r\n- Script sequencing matters: capture Outbox baselines before `createGroup`; enable `allowMemberMute` before member mute\r\n and do it before mute-all; review-list members must be normal, roleType=0, and unmuted. `member:index` materialization\r\n is P3-C2 and is expected to be absent in P3-A4~A7. [Task 2]\r\n- Phase 4 v0.3 covers PROFILE_SUMMARY/FULL/STATS, GROUP_PROFILE/STATS, FRIEND_VIEW, and GROUP_MEMBER_VIEW. Private view\r\n uses field-level complete envelopes and Lua CAS rather than an owner manifest; new `*_V2` Outbox relation types isolat\r\ne rolling releases; JSON/field envelopes use `SHA256_CANONICAL_JSON_V1`, while Set domains retain `SUM128_V1`. [Task 3]\r\n- Safety fences are mandatory for privacy/history-sensitive changes: set before DB fact changes; a failure to acquire m\r\nust block commit; fences clear only via the matching higher-version commit or mutationId-scoped REPAIR. `ConversationSe\r\nrviceImpl#resolveGroupJoinTimeEpoch` must fail closed when joinTime is unavailable, not skip history filtering. All rea\r\nders/processors must recognize fences and `*_V2` types before writers are enabled. [Task 3]\r\n- Phase 0-4 retain compatibility through old+new writes, SHADOW dual-read, and default-false domain-read switches; Phas\r\ne 5 is the “断旧” point. A dev pass does not waive Cluster same-slot proof, seven-day SHADOW zero difference, fail-clos\r\ned/rollback drills, reconciliation tamper test, DBA version-row capacity, or P1 performance gates. [Task 4][Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- A post-create Outbox baseline causes false timeout because the create transaction has already inserted records; sampl\r\ne first. Do not put braces in legacy-key checks, and SKIP unimplemented P3-C2 member-index assertions. [Task 2]\r\n- A contract with an unproven atomic algorithm, reused Outbox type that old processors can prematurely complete, weak J\r\nSON checksum, or privacy-expanding default is not ready to pass static review. Close those blockers before declaring pa\r\nss. [Task 3]\r\n- `apply_patch` Add File needs a blank `+` line immediately after the header or it can fail with `invalid hunk ... is n\r\not a valid hunk header`. In PowerShell, use `rg 'pattern' docs/architecture -g '*.md'`, not `docs/architecture/*.md` (o\r\ns error 123). [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM conversation-list 500 from conv:last cache corruption\r\nscope: Diagnose a missing friend-approval message when a participant's IM conversation list fails; use for Redisson `HG\r\nETALL` decode errors, `conv:last` anomalies, and cache-first remediation design.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=affected users, keys, logs, dev host\r\n, and branch `sprint3-0826-147` are time-specific; the per-user list verification, bad-key scan, and three-layer fix ar\r\ne reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Separate welcome-message delivery from the conversation-list 500 and locate corrupt conv:last keys\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-44-53-a2qD-im_convlast_cache_corruption_list500_friend_approval_welcome.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-202\r\n6-08-20T13-44-53-01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T09:18:02+00:00, thread_id=01a01db3-6\r\nd5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b, partial: cache deletion and self-heal verified; durable read/write hardening documented, no\r\nt implemented)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 好友申请通过, 消息列表不显示, 会话列表500, conv:last, ConversationServiceImpl, getRecentConversationList, readAllMap,\r\n HGETALL, CommandDecoder, JsonJacksonCodec, InvalidTypeIdException, RBatch, batchCacheLastMessage, applyLastMessageFall\r\nback, hlen!=3\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Produce the three-layer production investigation and repair plan\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-44-53-a2qD-im_convlast_cache_corruption_list500_friend_approval_welcome.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-202\r\n6-08-20T13-44-53-01a01db3-6d5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-21T09:18:02+00:00, thread_id=01a01db3-6\r\nd5a-70a2-ac77-3c4429898d1b, success: production investigation and repair runbook delivered; per-environment scan and ap\r\nproval still required)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IM-会话列表500-会话最后消息缓存损坏-修复方案.md, hlen=3, readAllMap try/catch, applyLastMessageFallback, Redis SCAN, \r\nRBatch 并发异步命令, 87c737e1e, 86f848291, X-User-Id\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when defining the message behavior, the user corrected “方向错了，是A加B，B同意后，给A发消息：你好，我是B ... 且A消息\r\n列表1条未读” -> do not invent bilateral system messages; preserve the requested B→A direction and receiver-side unread \r\nsemantics. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user says “大白话介绍给我” / “大白话解释” -> explain the causal chain with a plain-language analogy before t\r\nhe technical details. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- when the user asks “生产也存在这个问题啊，我怎么排查” -> give a step-by-step, executable production runbook: reproduc\r\ne with user identity, inspect HGETALL/CommandDecoder logs, scan all keys, identify affected users, stop the bleeding, t\r\nhen deploy the durable fix. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- First validate each participant independently. In this incident, the B→A welcome message was already persisted and A'\r\ns list worked; B's list returned a business 500 because an unrelated old group `conv:last` cache entry failed to decode\r\n. Do not equate a missing UI item with a failed message-generation chain. [Task 1]\r\n- `ConversationServiceImpl.getRecentConversationList` calls `redissonClient.getMap(key).readAllMap()` inside a stream w\r\nithout per-conversation protection. A decode exception from one `conv:last` key bubbles through `GlobalExceptionHandler\r\n`, so one bad cache entry takes down the complete list even though `applyLastMessageFallback` can rebuild a normal cach\r\ne miss from `TB_MESSAGE`. [Task 1]\r\n- Expected key is `yopu:im:conv:last:{userId}:{sessionId}:{scope}` (`scope` 0 public, 1 private) with exactly three quo\r\nted hash fields: `\"msgType\"`, `\"content\"`, `\"sendTime\"`. A practical non-mutating detector is a Redis `SCAN` over `yopu\r\n:im:conv:last:*` and `HLEN`; investigate `hlen!=3`, especially ETX-prefixed/UTF-8-truncated field names. Never carry a \r\ndevelopment scan result into production: rescan each environment. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- Deleting a confirmed corrupt `conv:last` key is cache-only stop-the-bleeding: the next read invokes `applyLastMessage\r\nFallback`, reads the last message from DB, and repopulates the normal 30-day TTL cache. Verified in dev, but production\r\n deletion requires a freshly verified key list and authorization. [Task 1]\r\n- Durable repair has three layers: A delete confirmed bad cache keys; B wrap `readAllMap` with per-key `try/catch`, war\r\nn with user/session/key, evict and fall back to DB; C replace the remaining `ConversationServiceImpl.batchCacheLastMess\r\nage` two-step RBatch write path with concurrent async commands, consistent with the related `87c737e1e` repair. The RBa\r\ntch issue is strongly suspected, not fully proven as the unique writer root cause. [Task 2]\r\n- The user's earlier account-side `86f848291` welcome-message reliability change is not the cause: it makes B→A deliver\r\ny reliably triggered/idempotent; it does not repair a corrupt list-preview cache. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Symptom: one party sees the conversation and the other does not. Initial mistake: attribute it to missing “通过” mess\r\nage generation or propose bilateral welcome messages. Fix: call both users' list endpoints and inspect business status \r\nbefore changing delivery logic; then follow message DB, session index, and list/cache data separately. [Task 1]\r\n- Symptom: a request looks successful at HTTP level but client behavior is a list failure. Cause: the API can carry bus\r\niness `code=500` even when transport is HTTP 200. Fix: inspect the application response body and server logs, not HTTP \r\nstatus alone. [Task 1]\r\n- A large `apply_patch` document failed with `is not a valid hunk header` because an added line lacked `+`. For a large\r\n MD repair plan, ensure every new line in an added hunk has the prefix or split the document into smaller, checkable pa\r\ntches. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-im-core message-collection USED_BYTES quota repair and test backfill\r\nscope: Repair media collection quota accounting when displayed used space stays at 0B, and safely backfill the test dat\r\nabase after contract-aligned code validation.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=server addresses, branch, target use\r\nr, and current schema are environment-specific; the physicalBytes settlement, atomic quota, and backfill verification r\r\nules are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Repair final physical-byte settlement and permanent media rejection\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T11-18-11-HAhd-yopu_im_message_collection_used_bytes_quota_fix_and_backfill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollo\r\nut-2026-08-20T19-18-11-01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T11:36:39+00:00, thread_id=01a0\r\n1ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03, success: focused tests and package passed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 消息收藏, 已用空间, USED_BYTES, RESERVED_BYTES, convertReservedToUsed, physicalBytes, settlePhysical, completeMediaTa\r\nsk, FILE_TOO_LARGE, QUOTA_BYTES_EXCEEDED\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Execute and verify 32-shard test-database USED_BYTES backfill\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T11-18-11-HAhd-yopu_im_message_collection_used_bytes_quota_fix_and_backfill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollo\r\nut-2026-08-20T19-18-11-01a01ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T11:36:39+00:00, thread_id=01a0\r\n1ee4-93b1-7932-873a-261aceb63f03, success: 32-shard backfill executed; mismatch=0)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- TB_MESSAGE_COLLECTION_QUOTA, MEDIA_BYTES, READY, 32 分片, 消息收藏配额_USED_BYTES_回填.sql, 172.21.131.79, 139.196.23\r\n.165, releaseUsed, mismatch\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user supplied a closed root cause and asked “要我按这个方案直接改吗？①③ 涉及代码 + ② 需要执行到 test 库” -> \r\ndirectly implement the smallest contract-aligned change, run the backfill, and verify; do not regress to a design discu\r\nssion, and report code changes versus test-database writes separately. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- when the user cited “physicalBytes 为最终大小；IM 按它结算全局物理容量与用户逻辑配额” -> use the contract document as\r\n the repair authority, not a surface workaround. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user specified “② 需要执行到 test 库” -> confirm access path and shard semantics, make a read-only precheck,\r\n then write and immediately verify both the target user and all shards. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- The 0B root cause was a semantic mismatch: image/video content has no `size`, while `CollectionSnapshotBuilder.extrac\r\ntSize()` recognizes only `size/fileSize/bytes`; therefore reservation and used bytes could be 0. `MediaCopyResult.Snaps\r\nhot.physicalBytes` is available after copy completion and `markReady` writes `MEDIA_BYTES`, so completion-time user quo\r\nta must settle final physical bytes, consistent with `settlePhysical`. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not merely replace `reservedBytes` with `totalBytes`: estimated > final leaves too much `RESERVED_BYTES`, and rese\r\nrvation=0/final>0 skips atomic capacity enforcement. Use `convertReservedToUsed(userId,count,reservedBytes,finalBytes)`\r\n: add `finalBytes`, subtract only `reservedBytes` with `GREATEST`, and enforce `USED_BYTES + GREATEST(RESERVED_BYTES-re\r\nservedBytes,0)+finalBytes <= QUOTA_BYTES` in the same update. Text uses `(0L,0L)`. [Task 1]\r\n- `completeMediaTask` rejects each snapshot over `maxSingleFileBytes` as `FILE_TOO_LARGE`; zero rows updated means `QUO\r\nTA_BYTES_EXCEEDED`. Both are permanent Worker outcomes and must `failAndCleanup`, not retry. Focused command passed 15 \r\ntests: `mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am test \"-Dtest=MessageCollectionTaskPersistenceServiceTest,CollectionSnapshotBui\r\nlderTest\" \"-DfailIfNoTests=false\" \"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\"`; package also passed. [Task 1]\r\n- Backfill authority is `USED_BYTES = SUM(MEDIA_BYTES)` from READY collection rows per shard; keep `RESERVED_BYTES` unc\r\nhanged, matching deletion `releaseUsed`. Use `yopu-im/yopu-im-core/src/main/resources/sql/dml/消息收藏配额_USED_BYTES_\r\n回填.sql`; success requires an all-shard `USED_BYTES <> COALESCE(READY SUM(MEDIA_BYTES),0)` mismatch count of 0. [Task \r\n2]\r\n- Only verified test DB access was jump host `139.196.23.165` (db-server01) to `172.21.131.79:3306`; local machine and \r\ndev nodes could not connect. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- A large patch failed because the expected Worker context was inaccurate -> apply small focused patches and reread eac\r\nh target before patching. [Task 1]\r\n- Local PyMySQL timed out and SSH to `10.168.1.232` was rejected -> never report a backfill as executed until a reachab\r\nle jump host performs it and post-write verification succeeds. [Task 2]\r\n- Inline multiline `python -c` in PowerShell broke quoting/newlines -> use uploaded SQL with remote mysql, or assemble \r\none remote command string. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-crm-account friend authorization snapshot async repair and delete-friend late\r\nncy diagnosis\r\nscope: Review, implement, test, and runtime-assess the FRIEND authorization-snapshot async path; diagnose friend deleti\r\non latency without overstating incomplete trace evidence.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=dev hosts, metrics, branch, and line\r\n locations are time-specific; the outbox ordering, executor, and trace-evidence rules are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Repair slow friend-request acceptance with ordered FRIEND snapshot async work\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T02-21-44-diyk-yopu_friend_request_accept_async_im_snapshot_fix.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\\r\nYeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-2\r\n0T10-21-45-01a01cf9-716e-7cd0-9b2c-6f7a8ede5750.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T09:58:07+00:00, thread_id=01a01cf9-716e-7c\r\nd0-9b2c-6f7a8ede5750, success: repaired and 360 tests passed; runtime Trace evidence remains unavailable)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 好友申请同意慢, CacheInvalidationOutboxWriter, imSnapshotExecutor, accountAsyncExecutor, CallerRunsPolicy, ImRelation\r\nAuthorizationSnapshotProjector, AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE, afterSnapshotReady, outbox_pending_oldest_seconds\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Diagnose 3–5 second delete-friend latency from code and dev metrics\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T02-21-44-diyk-yopu_friend_request_accept_async_im_snapshot_fix.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\\r\nYeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-2026-08-2\r\n0T10-21-45-01a01cf9-716e-7cd0-9b2c-6f7a8ede5750.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T09:58:07+00:00, thread_id=01a01cf9-716e-7c\r\nd0-9b2c-6f7a8ede5750, partial: code/metrics diagnosis complete; same-trace proof pending)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- deleteFriend, POST /user/social/friend/delete, crmPrivateFeign.cancelFriendByDelete, clearSessionMsg, FRIEND_VIEW, X-\r\nTrace-Id, actuator/metrics, /actuator/logfile 401\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Close the production delete-friend root cause, implement async snapshots, and dev-verify\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- deleteFriend, POST /v1/user/social/friend/delete, FRIEND, FRIEND_VIEW, CacheInvalidationOutboxWriter, imSnapshotExecu\r\ntor, afterCommit, 661171e9-8c51-408a-8c2a-2ec7a44c1bb9, 376 tests, 10.168.1.233:9001\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked for “方案评审”, then “补强后评审”, then “你来补强” -> first do a strict document-only review; onc\r\ne asked, directly rewrite the design document rather than waiting for the user to edit it. [Task 1]\r\n- when asking “改动范围大吗” and “生产才800用户不到，就会卡那么长时间” -> state change size/risk and explain the concre\r\nte latency mechanism; do not equate a small user count with a fast request. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user said “我改完了，是否通过测试” -> compare the diff with the approved design, then run module tests plus \r\na clean rebuild rather than relying on incremental compilation. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user said “删除好友，大约3-5秒” and “排查一下” -> begin with a no-data-change investigation (metrics, health\r\n, source call chain), not by deleting test relations or changing data. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- `acceptFriendRequest` afterCommit work was still in the HTTP thread: about 18 DB plus 20 Redis round trips for two au\r\nthorization rebuilds, two friend views, fence/JetCache clearing, and Outbox state. Keep the fix narrow: a dedicated `im\r\nSnapshotExecutor` (4/8/500/`AbortPolicy`), only FRIEND afterCommit work uses `submitFriendRebuild`, and `RejectedExecut\r\nionException` leaves an Outbox fallback; other Outbox types stay synchronous. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not reuse `accountAsyncExecutor`: its 2/5/200 `CallerRunsPolicy` can return slow rebuild to the request thread. `i\r\nmmediateRebuildFriend` returns success and only then runs `afterSnapshotReady`; welcome messages require snapshots rebu\r\nilt and fences cleared first, otherwise REDIS_ONLY `authorizeSingleChat` returns `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE` and messag\r\nes can be silently lost. [Task 1]\r\n- Outbox is fixed-delay 60s with claim/lease and retry, so “60s 内必达” is not hard acceptance; use `outbox_pending_old\r\nest_seconds<120s`, `FAILED=0`, and rejection count 0. Diff matched the design; module then clean test passed 357 and la\r\nter suite reached 360. [Task 1]\r\n- Production trace evidence closed the diagnosis: `deleteFriend` registered 1× FRIEND plus 2× FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds as s\r\nerial synchronous `afterCommit` work in the HTTP thread; the two FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds dominated (~0.94s), making accoun\r\nt deletions average ~2.69s. Private cancel (~11.5ms) and IM clear (~7.5ms) were not the cause. [Task 3]\r\n- The implemented boundary is a dedicated configurable `imSnapshotExecutor` (default core/max/queue `4/8/500`, `AbortPo\r\nlicy`): FRIEND and FRIEND_VIEW rebuilds are submitted after commit; rejection logs and leaves the Outbox PENDING for co\r\nmpensation instead of falling back to the request thread. Keep immediate JetCache friend-list eviction synchronous for \r\nread-after-write consistency. [Task 3]\r\n- The welcome message may run only after snapshot rebuild, fence clearing, and Outbox COMPLETED; use `afterSnapshotRead\r\ny`, not the transaction callback itself. Dev real-chain test (login → request → accept → delete → list) showed 97–124ms\r\n deletes, immediate empty lists on both sides, and no `AUTH_SNAPSHOT_UNAVAILABLE`/queue-full/welcome-send failures. Pro\r\nduction still needs 3–5 smoke samples ≤300ms and ≥20-request P95 before release. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- The initial plan made all seven Outbox categories asynchronous and did not preserve welcome-message/snapshot order ->\r\n minimize the async surface and model cross-thread order explicitly. [Task 1]\r\n- Earlier dev-only metrics could not prove the 3–5s production report. Pivot to production read-only evidence: the late\r\nr same-trace log timeline closed the cause without mutating data; where `mysql` is absent, do not invent Outbox state b\r\neyond trace evidence. [Task 1][Task 2][Task 3]\r\n- Large Maven output was truncated -> continue via streaming `write_stdin(session_id)` rather than treating a truncated\r\n response as the result. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / yopu-im-core Redis authorization RBatch concurrency risk and reproduction plan\r\nscope: Assess whether authorization snapshot reads should become concurrent/asynchronous, distinguish supported RBatch \r\nevidence from unproven claims, and prepare a safe preproduction reproduction plan.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=test commit, Redis addresses, and li\r\nve pool configuration are environment-specific; fail-closed authorization and evidence-tier rules are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Assess authorization-reader async risk and test-branch Batch evidence\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-49-30-zy3T-im_redis_batch_concurrency_risk_assessment_and_plan_doc.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wor\r\nkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-20\r\n26-08-20T13-49-30-01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T06:13:40+00:00, thread_id=01a01db7-\r\na702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791, success: read-only assessment and documented reproduction plan; no production-code change)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader, RBatch, createBatch, BatchOptions.defaults, executeAsync, CommandDecoder, Messag\r\neAckService, fail-closed, FENCE_RETRY_DELAYS_MS, c5dcdcfd\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Define preproduction mixed-load reproduction and conditional severity\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-20T05-49-30-zy3T-im_redis_batch_concurrency_risk_assessment_and_plan_doc.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wor\r\nkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\20\\rollout-20\r\n26-08-20T13-49-30-01a01db7-a702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-20T06:13:40+00:00, thread_id=01a01db7-\r\na702-74d2-ac1c-a97173e1b791, success: document added before authorized isolated-account execution)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IM Redis Batch 并发风险复现与定级方案-20260820.md, BATCH_RACE_, REDIS_ONLY, connectionPoolSize 512, 500/1500/2500 QPS\r\n, cmd5=cmd6=cmd27=cmd7, ackPending, Outbox\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asks only “这个如果改为并发异步，是否有风险” -> do read-only source verification and a risk conclusion \r\nfirst; authorization/security paths remain fail-closed and do not become low risk because the diff is small. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user shows a review screenshot about `test` Batch residue -> verify named-branch source with `git show`/`git\r\n grep`, not only the working tree; distinguish stronger screenshot claims from what repository evidence proves. [Task 1\r\n]\r\n- when asking “这个影响很大吗，评估风险” -> assess probability × impact scope × possible unauthorized access and make s\r\neverity conditional: reproduced P0, historical-comment-only P1 high risk, unreproduced ordinary-command claim inconclus\r\nive. [Task 1]\r\n- when choosing “复现与定级” but saying “先落方案md” -> write the reviewable plan before preproduction traffic; isolate\r\nd accounts and `BATCH_RACE_<runId>` are prerequisites. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Reader methods use one `RBatch` with multiple `getAsync` and one `batch.execute()`, so each authorization decision is\r\n one network round trip. `executeAsync()` does not improve latency if callers still await authorization. Fence, ready/v\r\nersion, membership, and blacklist remain a single fail-closed consistency window. [Task 1]\r\n- `MessageAckService` documents concurrent RBatch contention, response misalignment, and `CommandDecoder` failures; ACK\r\n changed to ordinary `setAsync`. It does not prove any ordinary command concurrent with any Batch always misaligns. At \r\ntest/origin-test commit `c5dcdcfdf15f8f069592acc24afef764bf01a4f4`, 13 `createBatch()` calls remain, including four aut\r\nhorization reads. [Task 1]\r\n- Treat possible single-chat blacklist empty-set behavior as theory, not a confirmed bypass. Runtime `RedisConfig` can \r\noverride YAML 64 with pool 512/min-idle 10; confirm effective pool and `REDIS_ONLY` from logs/metrics. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- Plan file `docs/architecture/IM Redis Batch 并发风险复现与定级方案-20260820.md` uses 500/1500/2500 QPS mixed load wit\r\nh ten-minute steady tiers. P0 requires `cmd5==cmd6==cmd27==cmd7==planned`, zero lost/duplicate/outOfOrder, `ackPending=\r\n0`, MQ/Outbox drained. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- “Many Redis calls” is not proof that authorization needs async concurrency -> measure RBatch latency, pool waits, and\r\n processor queue/rejections first. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not assume YAML 64 pool or inevitable ordinary-command misalignment; do not broadly replace Batch or split authori\r\nzation into concurrent GETs before reproduction. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Codex archived-session analysis and PowerShell variable-stripping workaround\r\nscope: Group and summarize archived Codex sessions in Chinese, while avoiding the local inline PowerShell `$`-variable \r\nexecution trap.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=archive IDs, titles, statuses, and dates are a historical snapshot\r\n; the archive-query API and 