ed script is `add_adaptation_v2_subtitles.py`, not its older `add_subtitles.py`. [Task 1]\r\n- Series workflow is source text → visual memory sentence → four-frame admission (01/03/10/20) → topic card → 20-image \r\nstoryboard; do not write the formal 20-image storyboard before the four-frame direction passes. S3《画工画僵尸》 is at \r\nlocked visual/20-image draft, pending formal generation; `S3/images/visual_test/` is ignored. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- `origin/HEAD` is unset here; compare explicitly with `origin/story`. If upstream history has same-title/different-has\r\nh commits, use `git diff --name-status` or `git diff-tree --no-commit-id --name-status -r` rather than slow `git diff -\r\n-stat`. For add/add conflicts, inspect `:2:` and `:3:` before taking a side. [Task 2]\r\n- If large historical blobs make a safe push time out, first estimate `origin/story..HEAD` object bytes with `git rev-l\r\nist --objects` + `git cat-file -s`. After verifying the desired tree, make a one-commit tree on the remote tip via `git\r\n commit-tree <tree> -p <remote_tip>` and `git reset --soft`; prove `git diff <oldHEAD> HEAD --stat` is empty before fas\r\nt-forward push. Increase push timeout only after shrinking history if needed. [Task 2]\r\n- The episodes state machine is `IDEA_LOCKED → STORYBOARD_LOCKED → VISUAL_CALIBRATED → PRODUCTION_PASSED → PUBLISH_READ\r\nY → PUBLISHED → DATA_REVIEWED`; transitions are adjacent-only and auto-validate before state changes. Use `episode_stat\r\ne.py init/show/transition`, `validate_episode.py <dir> [--target X] [--all]`, and `test_validator.py`. `episode-state.j\r\nson` is authoritative over README prose. [Task 3]\r\n- Import a delivery package by inspecting its original nested path and a prior import commit, flattening it into the ma\r\ntching existing series, renaming it to match the story, updating root/episodes/series/system indexes, and spot-checking\r\n `SHA256SUMS` with `Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256`. Stage tracked changes via `git add -u` plus the new directory, the\r\nn `git push origin story`; do not stage ignored package images. [Task 3]\r\n- The media whitelist permits `episodes/**/assets/characters/**`, `research/competitors/**`, and `research/account/**`;\r\n binary/media extensions are otherwise ignored. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- `git rebase --autostash origin/story` can fail because ignored, untracked images would be overwritten. Abort it, pres\r\nerve the worktree, and use a controlled merge/conflict resolution or the verified tree-rewrite route; never delete the \r\nignored media merely to make rebase succeed. [Task 2]\r\n- Removing files from the index does not remove their old blobs: a push can still contain ~GB of past `images`/ZIP data\r\n. Measure outgoing objects and squash/reparent only after tree-equivalence verification. [Task 2]\r\n- A prior subtitle comparison used the wrong S1/S2 sources. Final-script identification is a required first check; docs\r\n drafts and old helpers are not proof of published text. [Task 1]\r\n- Delete/rename cleanup can leave root README links stale: after removing a template or changing a package path, `rg` t\r\nhe repository for old references and repair every index. [Task 3]\r\n- `Remove-Item -LiteralPath ... -Force` is blocked by policy in this environment. For an obsolete package directory, us\r\ne reversible `Move-Item` to `D:\\codex-img\\<series>_<old-name>_废弃` instead. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM service-split Phase 0 planning and review\r\nscope: Produce and strictly review the document-only Phase 0 boundary, single-write, reliable-event, rollback, and acce\r\nptance plan before any IM service code split.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=source locations, branch baseline, c\r\napacities, and infrastructure observations are checkout-specific; the Phase 0 gates and correctness invariants are reus\r\nable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Draft and review the single-chat optimization/service-split direction\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-19T07-35-42-ZCGO-im_service_split_phase0_plan_review.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpa\r\nce\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\19\\rollout-2026-08-19T15-35-42-01\r\na018f2-8785-7120-a3b1-9c55a592cdbe.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T07:00:23+00:00, thread_id=01a018f2-8785-7120-a3b1-9c55a\r\n592cdbe, success: direction and Phase 0 plan conditionally approved; no business code changed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IM服务拆分Phase0实施与评审方案-20260824.md, IM单聊下一阶段优化与服务拆分落地方案-20260819.md, Phase 0, P0-01, P0-03, \r\nP0-04, Access, Store, Deliver-ACK, Session, Push, Group, Relation, 字段级单写, Result Outbox, sessionId, shardUid, ORIG\r\nIN_CONNECTION_ONLY, cmd=6\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked “帮我分析接下来的单聊优化方向，是否需要进行服务拆分，给我落成方案md” and then “方案评审” -> first\r\n deliver and strictly gate a reviewable architecture document; the authorization is document-only, not permission to ch\r\nange code, API, DTO, DB, or configuration. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user said “先落 Phase 0 实施方案并评审” and proposed Gateway/Receiver(Access)/Deliver/Store/Session/Group+Us\r\ner -> freeze boundaries before implementation and do not split all services at once. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Phase 0 is design-only: freeze boundaries, field-level single-write matrix, V1 contracts/reliable events, rollback sw\r\nitches, observability, reconciliation, and fault/contract tests. It does not create or deploy new services; only P0-01 \r\nthrough P0-03 may start, while P0-04 code refactoring is not authorized. [Task 1]\r\n- Target eight logical boundaries are Gateway/Access/Store/Deliver-ACK/Session/Push/Group/Relation. The first physical \r\nsplit is Access, Store, Deliver-ACK, Session, and Push; Group/Relation remains the CRM authority domain (`yopu-crm-acco\r\nunt`) and IM reads it through Feign/Redis authorization snapshots rather than copying the relation master database. [Ta\r\nsk 1]\r\n- Preserve four invariants: Store alone writes message facts; a conversation orders by canonical `sessionId` while `sha\r\nrdUid` is DB routing only; Store local transactions emit recoverable Reply/Delivery/Session results; `cmd=6` is `ORIGIN\r\n_CONNECTION_ONLY` and delivery cannot depend on the origin node surviving. For shared-hot-DB migration, enumerate old w\r\nriter/new writer/switch/rollback writer per field; a shadow path records differences but never writes. [Task 1]\r\n- Conditional-pass blockers: client/server must confirm original-connection `cmd=6`, group receive command and ACK rule\r\ns; DBA must approve session sequencing, durable idempotency and Result Outbox schema/index/retention; MQ/ops must confi\r\nrm RabbitMQ topology, Confirm/Return/retry/DLQ, partition migration and high watermarks; lock a baseline after assignin\r\ng existing uncommitted changes; define Snowflake workerId unique lease/renewal/collision stop before Access pre-generat\r\nes IDs. [Task 1]\r\n- Physical sequence: first Store (Session Worker co-deployed), then Deliver/ACK, then core converges to Access, then Se\r\nssion/Push; Group/Relation migration is a separate data project with single-write authority, historical migration, Outb\r\nox catch-up, dual-read checks, API cutover, and old-entry shutdown. [Task 1]\r\n- Current limits to account for: ordinary group delivery has no transactional Delivery Outbox (`buildAndSendGroupDelive\r\nryEvent` sends after commit), carries full `recipientUserIds`, uses 8 fixed partitions, writes every member's Session I\r\nndex, and ACK retry scans Redis Pending Keys under one global lock. Capacity evidence remains contextual: acceptance re\r\ndline is `cmd5==cmd6==cmd27==cmd7`, zero lost/duplicate/out_of_order/ackPending, and MQ/Result/Session Outboxes drained\r\n. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Treating multi-device idempotency as `clientType` alone can collide for two devices of the same type -> lock a real `\r\nrecipientEndpointKey` during P0-01. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not use “dual-node throughput nearly doubles” as a split or Phase 0 gate. It is only a post-split capacity observa\r\ntion; cross-node message correctness remains the release redline. [Task 1]\r\n- A compiling module is not proof that `chatDbAsyncExecutor` is safely injected: `IMServiceImpl` expects `RejectingExec\r\nutor`, while its Bean signature returns `Executor`/`ThreadPoolTaskExecutor` -> require context startup and saturated-qu\r\neue tests. Run `git diff --check` for plan edits; use quoted/LiteralPath PowerShell handling for Chinese paths. [Task 1\r\n]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / sprint test branch CRM local build, startup, and shutdown\r\nscope: Repair a broken local `test`-branch Maven build, start `yopu-crm-account` without registering a personal instanc\r\ne in shared Nacos, verify health, and stop only the target process.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\sprint\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=this is a distinct sprint che\r\nckout; commits, uncommitted fixes, services, ports, and dev endpoints are time-sensitive, while the build and PowerShel\r\nl shields are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Repair the local WIP build and start yopu-crm-account\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-24T10-04-58-3EK3-yopu_cloud_platform_fix_local_build_and_start_crm.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\r\n\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\sprint\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\24\\rollout-2\r\n026-08-24T18-04-58-01a0333a-f9c1-7302-a351-6533144f161f.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-24T10:20:19+00:00, thread_id=01a0333a\r\n-f9c1-7302-a351-6533144f161f, success: local build repaired; CRM started and `/actuator/health` was UP)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- yopu-crm-account, CrmAccountApplication, test, origin/test, dbebe5