:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\r\nss: live rule-mode attribution and traffic-control pivot established)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Clash Verge Rev, verge-mihomo, 127.0.0.1:9097, mixed-port 7897, /configs, /rules, /connections, MATCH,节点选择, profi\r\nles.yaml, rUwK2myX1tfT.yaml, GEOSITE,cn, OpenNetMeter\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Trace OpenCodex-to-ChatGPT uploads and lower replay context\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-09-38-JDVn-clash_opencodex_traffic_web_gpt_image_handoff_skill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\7\r\n9873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\14\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-09-38-019ffe08-3347-7b\r\n52-8094-015eaf08d979.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T06:10:44+00:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\r\nss: replay mechanism, cap limits, and image-work offload established)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- OpenCodex, bun.exe, chatgpt.com, metadata.sourcePort, Get-NetTCPConnection, openai_base_url, 127.0.0.1:10100, context\r\nCapValue, providerContextCaps, usage.jsonl, expandPreviousResponseInput, previous_response_id\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Move image generation to official web ChatGPT with a handoff skill\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-09-38-JDVn-clash_opencodex_traffic_web_gpt_image_handoff_skill.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\7\r\n9873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\14\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-09-38-019ffe08-3347-7b\r\n52-8094-015eaf08d979.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T06:10:44+00:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\r\nss: handoff skill, project rule, and vision-sidecar disablement applied)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- web-gpt-image-handoff, 官方网页ChatGPT, visionSidecar.enabled, AGENTS.md, image_gen, copy-ready handoff sheet, 10-per\r\n-batch\r\n\r\n## Task 4: Diagnose OpenCodex 401 account-pool and recurring 400 errors\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-20-26-xprg-opencodex_bun_proxy_error_diagnostics_401_oom_tool_state.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Us\r\ners\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\14\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-20-26-019ffe12-16\r\n40-76a0-a32f-77d9a287cb76.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-01T01:38:59+00:00, thread_id=019ffe12-1640-76a0-a32f-77d9a287cb76, \r\nsuccess: root causes separated and revalidated)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- CodexPoolAuthenticationError, 401 Unauthorized, chatgpt.com, wham/usage, usage.jsonl, service.log, Invalid JSON body,\r\n RangeError: Out of memory, Bun 1.3.14, Duplicate tool output for call_id, prompt_cache_retention, prompt_cache_options\r\n, Cloudflare challenge\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user says “我一直开的规则模式啊，你看看是不是配置有问题” -> do not start by blaming an accidental global-mod\r\ne switch; read live `/configs`, `/rules`, and the active profile binding before concluding. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asks “怎么去APP界面里面查询” -> provide a self-recheck path as well as the diagnosis. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user says “做调整” / “帮我改了” after a diagnosed, reversible fix -> apply it and verify the runtime result \r\ninstead of stopping at advice. [Task 1][Task 2]\r\n- when the user says “后面出图我只想用网页版本的gpt，给我方案” and “把这个落成skill” -> for AIGC image generation/edits\r\n, produce copy-ready prompt handoff sheets for official web ChatGPT; do not initiate image tools, browser automation, o\r\nr bulk media upload through Codex/OpenCodex. [Task 3]\r\n- when troubleshooting this machine, the user asks in Chinese why 401 persists despite free quota -> answer in Chinese \r\nand distinguish credential state, ChatGPT reachability, and quota up front. [Task 4]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Start with Clash `GET /configs`, `/proxies`, `/connections`, `/version`, and `/rules` at `http://127.0.0.1:9097`. A t\r\nerminal `MATCH,节点选择` in rule mode sends all non-domestic/unmatched traffic to the proxy: “局部” is domestic/allowli\r\nst routing, not only explicitly named sites. Use `connections[].chains` to distinguish DIRECT from a node. [Task 1]\r\n- To change a subscription's rules, first locate the active profile in `profiles.yaml` and its `option.rules` binding. \r\nOn this machine the effective file is `profiles/rUwK2myX1tfT.yaml`; adding `DOMAIN-SUFFIX,deepseek.com,DIRECT` and `GEO\r\nSITE,cn,DIRECT` to its `prepend` then restarting `clash-verge.exe` put GeoSite cn into live `/rules`. Global `Merge.yam\r\nl`, profile Merge `prepend-rules`, and core-only restart did not reliably rebuild the runtime configuration. [Task 1]\r\n- OpenNetMeter requires admin installation and records Clash-forwarded connections as `verge-mihomo`; query its `OpenNe\r\ntMeter.sqlite` `ProcessDate` joins for daily per-process totals, then use Clash `/connections` plus `metadata.sourcePor\r\nt` -> `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port>` -> process lookup to identify the real client. [Task 1]\r\n- Codex is routed through OpenCodex by `openai_base_url = \"http://127.0.0.1:10100/v1\"`. OpenCodex expands `previous_res\r\nponse_id` into full local input (`expandPreviousResponseInput`); the ChatGPT backend rejects that continuation ID, so i\r\nt repeatedly uploads full history. `contextCapValue` and every `providerContextCaps` in `C:\\Users\\79873\\.opencodex\\conf\r\nig.json` cap replay tokens, not network bytes; lowering 950000 to 200000 reduced but did not eliminate traffic. [Task 2\r\n]\r\n- For high-frequency image/story work through OpenCodex, start a new Codex task after a completed storyboard/chapter an\r\nd send reference images only when needed; long repeated sessions replay text and visual context. Web ChatGPT does not h\r\nave the same client-side replay amplification because its history stays server-side. [Task 2]\r\n- The durable image-work path is three layers: project `AGENTS.md` rule, global `web-gpt-image-handoff` skill, and `vis\r\nionSidecar.enabled=false`. The handoff includes per-frame positive prompt, locks, negatives, filename, and 10-image acc\r\neptance checklist; user generates/downloads manually in web ChatGPT. [Task 3]\r\n- For this proxy, `C:\\Users\\79873\\.opencodex\\usage.jsonl` is the fast status/model ledger and `service.log` is the erro\r\nr root-cause source. A 401 `CodexPoolAuthenticationError` means OpenCodex selected no usable account; first run account\r\n-state/WHAM checks and probe `chatgpt.com` via Clash. An active free account with remaining quota still fails when reac\r\nhability is `000`; WHAM 200/401 shows the API is reachable. Invoke `ocx.ps1` through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionP\r\nolicy Bypass -File ...` if execution policy blocks the shim. [Task 4]\r\n- Here `Invalid JSON body` was Bun request decoding after `RangeError: Out of memory`, not user JSON. Grep `service.log\r\n` for `request body decode/parse failed|panic\\(|Bun has crashed`; a ~950k context cap and giant sessions drove Bun 1.3.\r\n14 crashes. Start a new session, lower context caps to roughly 128k-256k, restart/upgrade OpenCodex, then monitor RSS. \r\n[Task 4]\r\n- `Duplicate tool output for call_id` points to client/proxy replay of a damaged session: stop retrying it, use a new t\r\nask, then restart/upgrade only if new tasks fail. `prompt_cache_retention is not supported on this model` is an auto-in\r\njected deprecated parameter; do not add it manually—upgrade the client to use `prompt_cache_options.ttl`. A Cloudflare \r\nchallenge HTML/403 from the homepage reflects the exit IP, not account quota; switch node/use a real browser and test t\r\nhe actual WHAM endpoint. [Task 4]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Editing global `Merge.yaml` and profile Merge before checking `profiles.yaml` wasted two attempts because neither fil\r\ne was compiled into live `/rules`; discover the bound custom-rule file first, then restart the Clash Verge application \r\nand verify `/rules`. [Task 1]\r\n- `verge-mihomo.exe -t -f clash-verge.yaml` can fail with `can't download MMDB: context deadline exceeded` when offline\r\n GeoIP/MMDB is absent; that does not prove a rule syntax failure when the running core already has the data. Validate l\r\nive `/rules` instead. [Task 1]\r\n- OpenNetMeter alone cannot distinguish direct from proxy traffic because it attributes both forwarded traffic to `verg\r\ne-mihomo`; do not stop at its process name—correlate the high-upload connection's source port and Clash chain. [Task 1]\r\n- A 200k replay cap is not a byte cap: multiple concurrent 200k+ context tasks can still consume GBs. For image/story r\r\nuns, switching the image step away from OpenCodex is the actual traffic-control pivot. [Task 2][Task 3]\r\n- Do not blame an expired subscription based only on `active_until`; this was initially wrong. Check `ocx account list \r\n--json --all` and live WHAM before attributing a 401 to account state. [Task 4]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / Douyin operations, subtitle review, topic research, and 05d regeneration\r\nscope: Browser-dependent Douyin metrics collection, subtitle QA, topic research boundaries, K1 comparison routing, and \r\nrelease-image validation for the story-production pipeline.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat; reuse_rule=follow current `standards/制作规范_正式版\r\n.md` and episode evidence; browser-config state and individual assets are time-specific.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Handle browser-blocked Douyin data collection and complete S1 subtitle review\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-12T05-59-04-OU27-douyin_data_browser_blocked_jsrepl_false_and_s1_subtitle_rev.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D\r\n:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-\r\n12T13-59-05-019ff48d-887c-73f3-98fc-f6b1b8cc22e3.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-14T14:59:51+00:00, thread_id=019ff48d-887c-7\r\n3f3-98fc-f6b1b8cc22e3, mixed: collection blocked; S1 subtitle review passed 20/20)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 抖音创作者中心, js_repl=false, Browser use requires privileged node_repl capabilities, browser-client.mjs, config.tom\r\nl, control-chrome, S1_墨脱, 带字幕评审, 数据验收报告\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Research Chang'e topic, route K1 comparison, and validate 05d release images\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-13T09-17-02-jAN1-shenshi_chang_e_topic_k1_comparison_05d_image_regen.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspa\r\nce\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-13T17-17-\r\n02-019ffa69-24cd-7022-848f-1622e2a0c8e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-14T10:46:12+00:00, thread_id=019ffa69-24cd-7022-848f-\r\n1622e2a0c8e7, partial: Chang'e topic approved; K1 scoring output missing; 05d has recorded drift)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 神尸系列, 嫦娥, 不要提到考古队, 对比K1泥人, 05d_神尸地图_嫦娥, 图10, 图11, 图17, 橙色反光条, 错位倒影, 现实侵入式伪纪\r\n录片\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user specifies “[@chrome] 用这个查看”, first check whether Chrome control is enabled; do not repeatedly retr\r\ny privileged browser paths after confirming `js_repl=false`. [Task 1]\r\n- for subtitles, “尽量不要放在右边、顶部和底部，不要遮挡主要信息” -> default to mid-left empty space, preserve the subj\r\nect, and check every character against storyboard text. [Task 1]\r\n- for 神尸系列, the user said “不要提到考古队了” and “网上找找，参考” -> avoid archaeology-team framing and actively re\r\nsearch comparable works while retaining a distinct hook. [Task 2]\r\n- for `对比打分`, require an explicit directory and target item (for example “对比K1泥人”) before scoring. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- First run `Select-String -Path \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.codex\\config.toml\" -Pattern \"js_repl\"`. If false, Chrome control ca\r\nnnot expose privileged `mcp__node_repl__js`; `browser-client.mjs` fails with `Browser use requires privileged node_repl\r\n capabilities`. Stop retries; Playwright without a Douyin login state cannot replace it. [Task 1]\r\n- `standards/数据验收报告.md` is the data-acceptance source. Keep views, likes, comments, favorites, shares, follows, a\r\nverage browse images, and swipe-away rate separate; do not use summary values as 24h/48h metrics. [Task 1]\r\n- S1's 20 subtitle images and `09_神话遗址_S1_墨脱_带字幕评审_V1.0.md` passed 20/20. Subtitle QA must catch generated w\r\nrong characters, as in 小尸镇在 / 遗蜕 / 涌过去. [Task 1]\r\n- The Chang'e topic may borrow only broad “moon-back relic / myth corpse / contact-driven collapse” structure. Avoid th\r\ne named 749局 hook set “集体自杀+同一句遗言+哥哥队长”; distinguish via distance mutation and the myth-corpse reveal. `r\r\neferences/zh-CN.md` / `en-US.md` are absent—use `standards/制作规范_正式版.md` as authority. [Task 2]\r\n- 05d's 20 release images passed file/timecode/subtitle continuity checks, but 图10's blue spacesuit stripe conflicts w\r\nith the orange-reflective-stripe rule and 图01's reflection remains centered rather than misaligned. Keep these as open\r\n drift; thumbnail subtlety is not acceptance. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Once `js_repl=false` is confirmed, do not repeat direct import/MCP-handshake/proxy-source experiments already documen\r\nted as blocked. [Task 1]\r\n- A K1 comparison inventory was cut off before a final scoring table: do not assert a final comparison score when the d\r\neliverable is absent. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Windows Codex desktop responsiveness, OpenCodex routing, and safe session archiving\r\nscope: Diagnose Codex UI/task-opening slowness versus model-response delay; safely reduce active-session index pressure\r\n without deleting user data.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=paths, process PIDs, file sizes, and OpenCodex configuration are m\r\nachine/time-specific; the diagnostic order and archive-first safeguards are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Diagnose Codex UI slowness and distinguish OpenCodex from client-side causes\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-11T15-08-06-uY5j-codex_slow_diagnostics_opencodex_session_cleanup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\7987\r\n3\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\11\\rollout-2026-08-11T23-08-06-019ff15d-d3fc-7e32-\r\n8050-def39a91b239.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-14T09:34:43+00:00, thread_id=019ff15d-d3fc-7e32-8050-def39a91b239, success:\r\n diagnosis and archive-first optimization)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Codex UI lag, task opening slow, OpenCodex, logs_2.sqlite, logs_2.sqlite-wal, sessions, archived_sessions, Get-Proces\r\ns, netstat -ano, Get-CimInstance, 127.0.0.1:10100, bun.exe, config.toml\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Archive inactive and oversized Codex sessions without deletion\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-11T15-08-06-uY5j-codex_slow_diagnostics_opencodex_session_cleanup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\7987\r\n3\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\11\\rollout-2026-08-11T23-08-06-019ff15d-d3fc-7e32-\r\n8050-def39a91b239.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-14T09:34:43+00:00, thread_id=019ff15d-d3fc-7e32-8050-def39a91b239, success:\r\n six oversized sessions archived and active sessions reduced 4.32GB to 0.81GB)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- codex_app__list_threads, limit: Too big: expected number to be <=50., codex_app__set_thread_archived, archived:true, \r\npinnedThreads, sessions 4.32GB, 0.81GB, image generation JSONL, complete exit, restart Codex\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user says \"是界面卡，进会话慢\" after an initial broad complaint, first distinguish UI/task-opening slowness \r\nfrom waiting for model responses before attributing a cause. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asks \"是不是opencodex或者其他导致我的codex卡呢\" -> treat OpenCodex as an independent hypothesis and sep\r\narate proxy/response-delay evidence from UI-rendering and local-index evidence. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asks \"有没有时间长不用的会话，帮我归档或者删除\" -> default to reversible archiving rather than deletion\r\n; explain the difference and preserve pinned, running, and currently relevant work. [Task 2]\r\n- when the user says \"你直接帮我优化\" after diagnosis is clear -> execute the smallest-risk optimization directly rathe\r\nr than prolonging analysis or asking again. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- For UI/task-opening slowness, inspect active `sessions` JSONL size and `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\logs_2.sqlite` before b\r\nlaming model/network latency. In this verified run, a 4.32GB active-session set and a 1.10GB log database were stronger\r\n suspects than OpenCodex; a small current task did not rule out global-index cost. [Task 1]\r\n- Oversized session space was highly concentrated: seven >=100MB files held about 86% of 4.22GB, mainly image-generatio\r\nn work. Prioritize a few large sessions rather than many <10MB sessions. [Task 2]\r\n- `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\config.toml` showed OpenCodex routing through `openai_base_url = \"http://127.0.0.1:10100/v1\"`;\r\n `netstat -ano` followed by a PID-filtered process query confirmed bun/OpenCodex on 10100. This proxy can affect respon\r\nse/send delay, but is not the leading explanation for task-opening/UI lag. [Task 1]\r\n- `codex_app__list_threads` accepts at most `limit:50`; inspect `pinnedThreads` and active `threads`, then archive usin\r\ng `codex_app__set_thread_archived({threadId, hostId:\"local\", archived:true})` and verify the task is absent from the ac\r\ntive list. Archiving moves JSONL from `sessions\\` to `archived_sessions\\`; it does not shrink `logs_2.sqlite`. [Task 2]\r\n- A safe successful intervention archived six oversized image/content tasks, reducing active sessions from 135 / 4.32GB\r\n to 129 / 0.81GB while retaining the current task, running work, pinned tasks, and IM tasks. Require a full Codex exit \r\n(including tray) and restart before judging UI improvement. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- `Get-CimInstance` WMI full-table queries repeatedly timed out locally. Use `Get-Process` plus `netstat -ano` for fast\r\n discovery; only then run `Get-CimInstance -Filter \"ProcessId=N\"` for a known PID. [Task 1]\r\n- PowerShell `foreach(){...} | Format-Table` produced `An empty pipe element is not allowed` -> collect results in `$ou\r\nt=@()` first, then pipe `$out` to formatting. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not delete or rebuild `logs_2.sqlite` while Codex is running: it risks corruption. A restart reduced WAL size in t\r\nhis run; any log maintenance belongs after a complete application exit. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Chinese employment DOCX generation with Codex documents and python-docx\r\nscope: Produce a formal, fillable Chinese Word document from a short request, with factual placeholders and structural \r\nQA when visual rendering is unavailable.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=the local documents-skill path, runtime Python, and LibreOffice av\r\nailability are machine-specific; the document/QA procedure is reusable for similar workplace DOCX deliverables.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Generate a formal employee probation-to-regularization application DOCX\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-12T02-48-51-cZJO-zhuanzheng_employee_probation_application_docx_documents_ski.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C\r\n:\\Users\\79873\\Documents, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-12T10-48-51-019ff3df-65c3\r\n-7720-a033-c9dd4f73784c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T02:53:39+00:00, thread_id=019ff3df-65c3-7720-a033-c9dd4f73784c, su\r\nccess: DOCX generated; structural and XML checks passed; visual rendering QA unavailable and disclosed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 给我写一份转正申请, documents, standard_business_brief, python-docx, LibreOffice, soffice, table_geometry.py, heading\r\n_audit.py, style_lint.py, a11y_audit.py, w:tblHeader, word/numbering.xml, PAGE, NUMPAGES, $OutputEncoding\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asks in Chinese \"给我写一份转正申请\" through the documents plugin -> deliver a real, formal, directly f\r\nillable Chinese `.docx`, not only prose or an outline. [Task 1]\r\n- for workplace documents without confirmed personal facts, use fields such as `【姓名】` and `【部门】` and do not tur\r\nn unfinished verification into a production/completed claim. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- The successful format used `standard_business_brief`: A4, Microsoft YaHei, 1.25 body line spacing, centered title, a \r\nbasic-information table, five body sections, signature area, independent numbered accomplishments/shortcomings, and a P\r\nAGE/NUMPAGES footer. [Task 1]\r\n- The local documents package was `C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\plugins\\cache\\openai-primary-runtime\\documents\\26.805.11740\\sk\r\nills\\documents`; its `table_geometry.py`, `heading_audit.py`, `style_lint.py`, and `a11y_audit.py` plus XML review veri\r\nfied the final document. `table_geometry.py <docx>` takes no `--check` flag. [Task 1]\r\n- `List Number` in python-docx does not itself create body `numPr`; real numbering requires `abstractNum`/`num` in `wor\r\nd/numbering.xml` and `w:numPr/w:numId` on paragraphs. For table width or header metadata, remove existing XML elements \r\nbefore appending replacements; duplicated `w:tblW`/`w:tcW` leaves stale values and breaks geometry checks. [Task 1]\r\n- If LibreOffice/`soffice` is unavailable, use the skill's structural/a11y/style audits and XML review as a fallback, b\r\nut explicitly state that render-level, page-by-page visual QA was not performed. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Piping Python through PowerShell with Chinese paths caused `PackageNotFoundError: Package not found at 'C:\\\\Users\\\\79\r\n873\\\\Documents\\\\????.docx'` -> set `$OutputEncoding = [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new()` before `| & $py -`. [Task 1]\r\n- PAGE/NUMPAGES fields may lack cached displayed values even though Word recalculates them; add a cached value and appl\r\ny consistent font to field runs for a more stable initial rendering. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM full-duplex JMeter, capacity acceptance, and reliability repair\r\nscope: Build and run real-user duplex WebSocket benchmarks, use closed-loop cmd=5/6/27/7 evidence for capacity acceptan\r\nce, and make narrowly tested IMServiceImpl reliability repairs.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=JMX and source paths are checkout-sp\r\necific; host addresses, runtime config, and all latency conclusions are run-specific.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Add configurable full-duplex continuous JMeter script\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T03-12-44-iX9Z-im_jmeter_duplex_pressure_test_handoff_and_bottleneck.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-\r\n30T11-12-44-019fb102-9517-7cc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-01T07:18:19+00:00, thread_id=019fb102-9517-7\r\ncc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7, partial: configurable JMX and cross-host P0 handoff)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- im_single_chat_duplex_continuous.jmx, java.net.http.WebSocket, -Jthreads, -JsendCountPerWindow, -JsendWindowSeconds, \r\ncmd=5, cmd=6, cmd=27, cmd=7, MissingPropertyException, DuplexListener\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Run 165-to-47 smoke and analyze cmd=27 latency\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T03-12-44-iX9Z-im_jmeter_duplex_pressure_test_handoff_and_bottleneck.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-\r\n30T11-12-44-019fb102-9517-7cc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-01T07:18:19+00:00, thread_id=019fb102-9517-7\r\ncc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7, success for the small P0, but not a capacity result)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 139.196.23.165, 172.20.196.192, 47.116.106.227, 172.20.196.193, ws://172.20.196.193:8084/ws, SingleChatPerformanceObs\r\nerver, [IM-PERF], cmd=6 P95 504ms, cmd=27 P95 459ms\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Prepare the requested rerun without contaminating the baseline\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T03-12-44-iX9Z-im_jmeter_duplex_pressure_test_handoff_and_bottleneck.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-\r\n30T11-12-44-019fb102-9517-7cc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-01T07:18:19+00:00, thread_id=019fb102-9517-7\r\ncc0-87d8-3b853a65e1e7, rerun requested; not yet executed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- pre RabbitMQ queue backlog, im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx, 47 health, current process configuration, cmd\r\n=27, baseline\r\n\r\n## Task 4: Re-run 2000 users across 165/75/89 and audit the 165-only comparison\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T10-33-53-Oz8h-im_2000_load_test_ack_reliability_repair.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWo\r\nrkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\03\\rollout-2026-08-03T18-33-54-0\r\n19fc72f-e9e4-7850-91d9-21fa6dee0bbd.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-05T07:21:03+00:00, thread_id=019fc72f-e9e4-7850-91d9-21fa\r\n6dee0bbd, partial: login passed but strict delivery closure and MQ/Outbox tail did not)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- matrix-2000-multi-20260803, matrix-2000-165-only-rerun-20260803, allLoginTimeoutMs, businessStartAt, no online friend\r\n target, cmd5=60000, cmd7=59786, ackPending, MQ/Outbox tail\r\n\r\n## Task 5: Repair ACK pending, duplicate retry, and offline delivery reliability\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-03T10-33-53-Oz8h-im_2000_load_test_ack_reliability_repair.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWo\r\nrkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\08\\03\\rollout-2026-08-03T18-33-54-0\r\n19fc72f-e9e4-7850-91d9-21fa6dee0bbd.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-05T07:21:03+00:00, thread_id=019fc72f-e9e4-7850-91d9-21fa\r\n6dee0bbd, partial: package and diff check passed; targeted tests were blocked by existing test-compilation errors)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IMHandler.handleMessageDeliverAck, MessageAckService.confirmAck, ackPending, OfflineMessagePersistenceService.persist\r\n, MessageConsumer, IMServiceImpl, cmd=7, IMServiceImplTest.java:[119,33]\r\n\r\n## Task 6: Execute the staged 200-to-2000 cross-machine concurrency matrix\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-01T05-38-50-uVTt-im_jmeter_matrix_2000_login_barrier_failure.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQia\r\nnWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-01T13-38-50-\r\n019fbbd5-1056-79b0-9022-6cf6d4b28573.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T10:18:33+00:00, thread_id=019fbbd5-1056-79b0-9022-6cf\r\n6d4b28573, failed at 2000 login readiness; 1500 short-window rerun passed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx, matrix-1500-rerun-20260803, matrix-2000-20260803, IM_LOGIN_CONNECT, IM_BU\r\nSINESS_CONTINUOUS_SEND, allLoginTimeoutMs, RabbitMQ ready/unack/consumers=0/0/8, Outbox\r\n\r\n## Task 8: Diagnose session-index contention and add Scheme B batch persistence observability\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T07-27-30-447s-im_chatdb_batch_observability_and_concurrency_capacity_plan.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\r\n\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026\r\n-08-06T15-27-30-019fd5f8-57e3-7bf2-ab2e-85ed77d6923e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-07T12:54:42+00:00, thread_id=019fd5f8-57\r\ne3-7bf2-ab2e-85ed77d6923e, partial: P1-A did not close Outbox; Scheme B compile/target-test evidence passed, but no rea\r\nl batch-load comparison)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- P1-A, P1-B, TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX, SessionIndexBatchApplyService, SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher, ChatDbBatchDispatc\r\nher, ChatDbBatchPersistService, IM-CHATDB-BATCH, IM-THREADPOOL, chatDbAsync, Outbox GAP, executor-pool-size\r\n\r\n## Task 9: Compare dev-im-merge and dev-imtest single-chat optimizations\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-07T08-18-48-u3KQ-compare_dev_im_merge_dev_imtest_single_chat_optimizations.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\w\r\norkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-0\r\n8-07T16-18-48-019fdb4d-aa58-7f90-a383-bc18159092f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-07T08:53:28+00:00, thread_id=019fdb4d-aa58\r\n-7f90-a383-bc18159092f4, success: static branch comparison and production-safe priority list; no runtime benchmark)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- dev-im-merge, dev-imtest, d7037b97bc77da196b47ef3130eaeda83a956575, JMeter, SingleChatPerformanceObserver, RBatch, Ab\r\nortPolicy, MessageConsumer, offline queue, DLQ, async DB, CPU affinity\r\n\r\n## Task 10: Verify the post-refactor single-chat chain and assess 2000 QPS readiness\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-07T02-35-59-YZSP-im_single_chat_chain_and_2000_qps_capacity_analysis.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspa\r\nce\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-07T1\r\n0-35-59-019fda13-d193-7921-9f3a-bdc8ddee8b0b.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-07T03:16:13+00:00, thread_id=019fda13-d193-7921-\r\n9f3a-bdc8ddee8b0b, partial: chain verified; 2000 QPS not strictly accepted)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IMHandler, messageProcessor, SingleChatPersistenceTask, chatDbAsyncExecutor, saveSingleMessage, SingleChatSessionOutb\r\noxPublisher, SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher, CallerRunsPolicy, clientMsgId, 2000-QPS, SelectorManager\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked to rerun and first check whether the current pre message queue still has backlog -> inspect relev\r\nant RabbitMQ Push, ACK/offline, and business queues read-only; establish a clear baseline before applying load. [Task 3\r\n]\r\n- when the user required “用户数量可配置、M秒发送N条可配置” -> expose workload controls as JMeter `-J` properties, not \r\nfixed constants. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user required login, heartbeat, and business commands to be reported separately -> keep protocol accounting \r\nand business TPS separate. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user corrected the host roles: \"165 作为纯粹的压力机，47是IM服务器\" -> confirm host role and private address\r\n before attributing CPU, network, or JVM evidence. [Task 2]\r\n- when the user asked to analyze the bottleneck first and \"不要盲目加线程\" -> add segment evidence before changing pool\r\n sizes. [Task 2]\r\n- when load exceeds 500, the user specified \"165 as the primary pressure host, then 75, 89\" -> state host roles and spl\r\nit ownership explicitly rather than distributing users arbitrarily. [Task 4]\r\n- when the user asked \"修复，然后看看还存在啥问题\" -> after each repair, audit remaining reliability gaps and distingui\r\nsh verified fixes from unverified risks. [Task 5]\r\n- when optimizing IM performance, the user required latest analysis and real load-test evidence, and rejected treating \r\nfinal drain or historical cumulative metrics as a steady-business-window conclusion -> distinguish business-window delt\r\nas from drain state and static/code evidence. [Task 8]\r\n- when comparing branches, the user asked what is different and what can be learned for single chat -> separate product\r\nion governance, load-test-only logic, and production-safe reusable changes; return a priority-ordered landing list rath\r\ner than a diff dump. [Task 9]\r\n- when planning batch execution, the user explicitly said “优先调整批量执行并发，不增大队列” -> change only `executor-p\r\nool-size` through 8, 16, then only if needed 24/32; do not jump to 32. [Task 8]\r\n- when judging 2000 QPS, the user continued to require strict protocol closure and actual evidence rather than login su\r\nccess or sender statistics -> require `cmd5=cmd6=cmd27=cmd7=planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`,\r\n and MQ/Outbox drain before making a capacity claim. [Task 10]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Before a rerun, confirm the pre RabbitMQ backlog is cleared or record its baseline, then verify 47 health, the deploy\r\ned JMeter file, and current process configuration. Historical backlog-induced `cmd=27` delay is not a capacity result f\r\nor the new run. [Task 3]\r\n- `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous.jmx` uses one long-lived JDK 17 WebSocket per real user; users both send and receiv\r\ne, targets are mapped after login, and the final summary records cmd=5/6/27/7, QPS/TPS, P50/P95/P99, delivery/ACK rate,\r\n loss, duplicates, and ordering. `users.json` has only 500 valid users, so larger runs require more real credentials an\r\nd friend mappings. [Task 1]\r\n- The validated cross-host P0 used 165=`139.196.23.165`/`172.20.196.192` as the JMeter pressure host and 47=`47.116.106\r\n.227`/`172.20.196.193` as the IM server. With two users at one message/user/second for 30 seconds, `cmd=5/6/27/7=60/60/\r\n60/60`, delivery/ACK were 100%, and loss/duplicates/out-of-order were zero: P0 only, not a capacity result. [Task 2]\r\n- `SingleChatPerformanceObserver` localized the gap to business execution through local Netty push write: cmd=6 P50/P95\r\n/P99=`489/504/748ms`, cmd=27=`449/459/663ms`, queued-to-executing is near zero, pushWritten is about 441–452ms, and pus\r\nhWritten-to-ACK about 3–5ms. Add segmented timing across persistence, routing, MQ publish/confirm, MQ consumer, and pus\r\nh before altering fixed pool sizes; socket writes remain on the channel EventLoop. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n- For the 2000-user three-host run, shard 165=1200, 75=500, 89=300 without overlap and confirm each shard has local onl\r\nine-friend targets. `allLoginTimeoutMs` must exceed the login ramp; 240s ramp with a 180s gate timed out, while a 360s \r\ngate passed login. Capacity acceptance requires login, business, final protocol aggregate, and MQ/Outbox tail together.\r\n [Task 4]\r\n- The 2026-08-03 three-host result is not a capacity pass: `cmd5=60000`, `cmd6/cmd27=59998`, `cmd7=59786` (2 missing me\r\nssages and 212 ACK gap); MQ/Outbox tail was not verified. The 165-only run also cannot support a strict 2000 msg/s clai\r\nm because staggered login compressed send time (`cmd5=57172`, `cmd6/cmd27=57167`, `cmd7=57165`). Rework the JMX into a \r\ntwo-stage model with shared `businessStartAt` and a fixed 30s business window after all users log in. [Task 4]\r\n- `IMHandler.handleMessageDeliverAck()` had marked receipt without `MessageAckService.confirmAck(userId,msgId)`, leavin\r\ng Redis pending keys and enabling duplicate direct pushes. The repair calls `confirmAck` for `cmd=7`; `IMServiceImpl` a\r\nnd `MessageConsumer` register pending before WebSocket write and cancel it on write failure; retry exhaustion/offline d\r\nelivery uses idempotent `OfflineMessagePersistenceService.persist` before clearing pending/retry keys. `MessageAckServi\r\nce` defaults observed in source: pending TTL 300s, max retry 3, Redis-key scan retry. Package validation (`mvn -pl yopu\r\n-im/yopu-im-core -am package \"-Dmaven.test.skip=true\"`) and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 5]\r\n- The matrix script is `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx`. A short-window result is acceptable only when logi\r\nn, business-send, final-summary, four-command closure, and MQ/Outbox tail all pass. `matrix-1500-rerun-20260803` met `1\r\n500/0` for main samples with MQ `ready/unack/consumers=0/0/8` and Outbox zero; retain the earlier 1000 login and 1500 b\r\nusiness failures as variability/reliability evidence. [Task 6]\r\n- `matrix-2000-20260803` used 2000 threads, 240s ramp, 30s business window, and 330s duration after zero MQ/Outbox gate\r\ns. Nineteen users did not reach a 180s login barrier; `IM_LOGIN_CONNECT 1981/0` was followed by `IM_BUSINESS_CONTINUOUS\r\n_SEND 1981/1981`. This is a load-generator/readiness failure, not a valid 2000-user IM-throughput result. [Task 6]\r\n- C0/C1 single-variable evidence identifies `TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX` UPSERT as the current 1000-QPS bottleneck: disablin\r\ng it changed cmd6 P50/P95 from 17.9s/39.4s to 69ms/108ms, restored about 999.8/s persistence, and reduced lock waits 99\r\n.7%. P1-A batch-local merge/sort by `(USER_ID, SESSION_ID)` reduces one-batch contention but is not cross-consumer key \r\nserialization. [Task 8]\r\n- P1-A is not accepted: business P50/P95 was 40/56ms but Outbox unapplied was 96,146 (53%); same-key cross-batch/cross-\r\nconsumer UPSERT contention remained. Use fixed-key partition serialization and bounded batching only after real P1-B lo\r\nad evidence. [Task 8]\r\n- Scheme B: `ChatDbBatchDispatcher` aggregates 50ms, groups `SHARD_UID % 32`, and defaults to an 8-thread per-shard exe\r\ncutor; `ChatDbBatchProperties.enabled=false`. `ChatDbBatchPersistService` writes messages and matching Outbox in one tr\r\nansaction, retries only routing/deadlock errors, then uses row-wise idempotent fallback. Watch `[IM-CHATDB-BATCH]` and \r\n`[IM-THREADPOOL]`; pre-production 96/128-thread settings do not validate production 24/48 with `chat-db=false`. [Task 8\r\n]\r\n- `dev-im-merge` is a production candidate baseline (thread/MQ isolation, bounded queues, `AbortPolicy`, optional CPU a\r\nffinity); `dev-imtest` is the stricter real-user JMeter/closed-loop observability system. Production-safe single-chat p\r\nriorities are: `RBatch` for login/heartbeat while preserving routing/online/TTL semantics, move heartbeat Redis work of\r\nf Netty workers and return explicit failure ACK on rejection, offline/DLQ fallback with `NACK(requeue=false)`, then min\r\nimize the persistence/session-index transaction. Async DB needs durable compensation and 500/1000-user A/B before enabl\r\nement; CPU affinity/pool expansion are later experiments. [Task 9]\r\n- Verified chain: Netty decode/auth -> `messageProcessor` authorization precheck -> `SingleChatPersistenceTask` on `cha\r\ntDbAsyncExecutor` / `im-asyncdb-` -> message main table plus session Outbox in the `saveSingleMessage` transaction -> l\r\nocal synchronous push or cross-node MQ (offline only when no online route) -> cmd6 ACK. The session index uses 16 seria\r\nl partitions, 150 records/50ms aggregation, ledger deduplication, batch upsert, and post-commit cache invalidation. Sou\r\nrce-default Outbox polling is 100ms but Nacos can override it at runtime. [Task 10]\r\n- The five-node 200 QPS x 120s run (23,994 messages) closed at aggregate 1000 QPS only; it cannot establish 2000 QPS or\r\n validate a high-single-host connection model. Use 1500 QPS x 180s for three all-zero rounds -> 2000 QPS x 180s -> 2000\r\n QPS x 10min for three all-zero rounds, with `CallerRuns=0`, stable P99, and no sustained MySQL/Redis/MQ saturation. [T\r\nask 10]\r\n- Prioritize bounded queues with fast rejection/explicit busy metrics over `CallerRunsPolicy`, restore transactional pe\r\nrsistent `(senderId, clientMsgId)` idempotency that returns the first `messageId`, then add segmented cmd6 metrics befo\r\nre tuning pools. Local synchronous push may reduce cmd27 but occupies `im-asyncdb-`; test the proposed independent boun\r\nded delivery executor with A/B evidence before claiming throughput gains. [Task 10]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not run directly when queue status, 47 health, JMeter artifact, or process configuration is unknown; do not attrib\r\nute an old queue backlog to the new run's capacity. [Task 3]\r\n- `DuplexListener` cannot read outer JMeter `props`: `groovy.lang.MissingPropertyException: No such property: props for\r\n class: DuplexListener` -> pass command configuration through shared listener state. [Task 1]\r\n- A failed early smoke can be a script/runtime issue, not an IM performance result: inspect JTL `responseMessage` and `\r\nlistenerError` first. For restarts, verify actual PID, 8084/8085, health, and `/actuator/beans` wiring for `singleChatP\r\nerformanceObserver`, not only the JAR filename. [Task 2]\r\n- `--spring.cloud.nacos.enabled=false` does not reliably suppress Nacos ConfigData import; a known recovery path explic\r\nitly supplies `--spring.config.import=optional:file:/opt/yopu-apps/conf/application-pre.yaml`, then verifies service he\r\nalth. Monitor RSS, Direct Memory, GC, and OOM before high-connection tests on 47 because `-Xmx50g + MaxDirectMemorySize\r\n=10g` leaves little headroom on 64G. [Task 2]\r\n- Do not call a run passed solely because all users logged in or a sender-side total looks complete. Require `cmd5 == c\r\nmd6 == cmd27 == cmd7 == planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`, and MQ/Outbox tail completion. [Tas\r\nk 4]\r\n- Do not claim the new ACK/offline tests passed: existing `IMServiceImplTest.java:[119,33]` and `[121,34]` fail test co\r\nmpilation because `isRetryableShardingRouteException(IllegalStateException)` is missing. Remaining risks: offline-persi\r\nstence failure retains only pending TTL, ACK misses are DEBUG-only, Redis full scans can cause retry bursts, and long J\r\nMeter runs do not reclaim `sent/byContent` maps. In PowerShell, quote whole Maven `-D` arguments. [Task 5]\r\n- When a 2000 run has incomplete login at the barrier, do not call the downstream business errors an IM capacity failur\r\ne. Increase/parameterize `allLoginTimeoutMs` beyond ramp/readiness, ensure every login thread can reach the barrier, an\r\nd collect target CPU/RSS/GC/EventLoop/connection and JMeter metrics before retrying. Do not begin 3000 until 2000 close\r\ns the full protocol and MQ/Outbox gates. [Task 6]\r\n- Do not equate MySQL global cumulative `Innodb_row_lock_waits` or `setAutoCommit -> socket read` with this run's row-l\r\nock cause: capture `BUSINESS_START/END` deltas and correlate `data_lock_waits`, `data_locks`, and `processlist`. `BUSIN\r\nESS_END` and `DRAIN_END` are separate; final queue=0 is not a steady-window pass. [Task 8]\r\n- The new `SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher` initially appeared patched but its file was absent -> after adding files, r\r\nun `Test-Path`/`Get-Item` before compiling. Its Maven package passed only with `-Dmaven.test.skip=true`; no P1-B load r\r\nesult exists. For a targeted reactor test, quote `\"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\"`; a normal `-DskipTests` bu\r\nild was blocked by existing `IMServiceImplTest` missing-method compilation. [Task 8]\r\n- Static branch comparison is not a JMeter/service/capacity run. Long Chinese paths can make `git show` fail; prefer sh\r\nort paths, `git diff --stat`, class-name search, or the working-tree file. Do not promote virtual users, auth bypasses,\r\n or virtual group members into production paths. [Task 9]\r\n- Do not treat local synchronous push's lower cmd27 as a throughput gain: first measure its long-lived occupancy of `im\r\n-asyncdb-` and the full protocol closure. If high single-host connection tests show duplicate/ACK-pending noise on Java\r\n HttpClient `SelectorManager`, distribute load generators and repair the login ramp/barrier before attributing readines\r\ns failure to the IM server. [Task 10]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM message-quote protocol and acceptance design\r\nscope: Review and document the server-side message-quote contract, persistence, invalidation, and compatibility rules; \r\nthis rollout did not implement business code.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck ImCommandConstant, IMHandler\r\n, gateway contracts, and the approved document before implementation.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Review and update the message-quote implementation/acceptance plan\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T07-11-07-7Fmu-im_message_quote_plan_review_and_protocol_update.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\\r\nYeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\30\\rollout-2026-07-30T15\r\n-11-07-019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-30T09:31:48+00:00, thread_id=019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b\r\n0b5-901078c5226e, success: design document reviewed and updated)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- content + extra + mentions, extra.replyTo.messageId, /v1/im/message/quote/target, ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, cmd=5\r\n, cmd=6, cmd=11, cmd=12, cmd=22, cmd=27, QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID, QUOTE_STATUS, MESSAGE_EXTRA, outbox\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked “具体要提供几个接口给客户端” -> state the count of new client APIs, changed existing contracts, c\r\nommand matrix, and acceptance evidence directly. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asked “补强后评审” and adopted `content + extra + mentions` -> expose blockers first, then make the use\r\nr's protocol the contract and strengthen server validation/state consistency around it. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- The approved shape is `content + extra + mentions`: client uploads only `extra.replyTo.messageId`; server generates t\r\nhe quote snapshot/status/version and returns `extra.replyTo` consistently in ACK, push, and history. `extra` needs vers\r\nion, whitelist, and size validation; reject or strip unknown fields. `mentions` remains a separate executable-semantic \r\nfield, with no @ business expansion this phase. [Task 1]\r\n- Protocol directions: single uplink `cmd=5`, ACK `cmd=6`; group uplink `cmd=11`, ACK/push `cmd=12`; single receive pus\r\nh `cmd=27`; revoke/quote invalidation `cmd=22`. String fast paths `handleSingleChat(String)` and `handleGroupChat(Strin\r\ng)` must parse nested `extra.replyTo.messageId`; use DTO + `ObjectMapper`, not hand-written JSON. [Task 1]\r\n- Add one original-message-location HTTP API, `/v1/im/message/quote/target`; the other four are existing payload-contra\r\nct changes, not five new APIs. Gateway `/v1/im/**` injects identity; never trust a client `userId`. Persist indexed `QU\r\nOTE_MESSAGE_ID`, `QUOTE_STATUS`, snapshot, and state version rather than scanning `MESSAGE_EXTRA`. [Task 1]\r\n- Revoke/cleanup is a separate cmd=22 `event` with `eventId`, `rootMessageId`, `stateVersion`, chunked affected quote I\r\nDs, `sequence`, and `lastChunk`; clients process idempotently. Keep hot-store updates atomic; use outbox/compensation f\r\nor cold store and ES rather than promising a global transaction. Capability downgrade must cover WebSocket, HTTP histor\r\ny/offline pull, and device Push. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not confuse uplink, ACK, receive push, and revoke event; verify `ImCommandConstant.java` and `IMHandler` before wr\r\niting the command matrix. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not mark all system messages non-quotable: freeze an allowlist by `msgType + content` subtype. Do not call design-\r\ndocument `git diff --check` success an implementation, DDL, Maven, or release verification. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Windows screenshot OCR for model-usage/cost questions\r\nscope: Extract model-usage data from a supplied Windows screenshot; use when a Chinese “今天花了多少钱/今日模型用量” re\r\nquest provides an image but no account entrypoint. Do not turn ambiguous OCR output into a precise cost claim.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=WinRT OCR availability and installed packages are machine-specific\r\n; the confidence and search-boundary safeguards are reusable.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: OCR a dark “今日模型用量” screenshot for DeepSeek cost\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- deepseek, 今日模型用量, OCR, Windows.Media.Ocr, WinRT, PowerShell, TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages, zh-Hans-CN, tes\r\nseract, cv2, control-chrome, mcp__node_repl__js, gray>150\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user attaches a dark screenshot and asks “deepseek今天花了多少钱” -> treat the screenshot as the primary dat\r\na source; start with local OCR and use a logged-in platform only when available, rather than first asking for an accoun\r\nt entrypoint. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- This machine has no tesseract/pytesseract/easyocr/paddleocr; Python 3.12 has PIL/cv2/numpy. The dependency-free optio\r\nn is `Windows.Media.Ocr` with `zh-Hans-CN`, after loading WinRT type projections and using generic `AsTask`/`Await`. [T\r\nask 1]\r\n- For a 185x225 dark image, `gray>150` and >4px row gaps separated the table header plus five rows. `control-chrome` ne\r\neds `mcp__node_repl__js`; without that tool, a logged-in Chrome fallback is unavailable. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- `Unable to find type` and `Cannot index into a null array` mean the WinRT types or generic `AsTask` method were not l\r\noaded: call `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Runtime.WindowsRuntime`, preload the required `[Windows...., ContentType=Win\r\ndowsRuntime]` types, and filter reflection with `$_.IsGenericMethod`. Use `TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages()` instead\r\n of an unloaded `Windows.Globalization.Language`. [Task 1]\r\n- Small dark-image numerals were inconsistent across OCR/enhancement attempts. If the number drives a cost decision, cr\r\noss-check multiple enhancements and manually inspect, or get source/platform data; do not report a single OCR result as\r\n exact. Bound any `rg` search to likely app directories and a timeout—recursing through `D:\\soft`/AppData was slow and \r\nirrelevant. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: Windows Fiddler Classic and MEmu HTTP/WebSocket capture setup\r\nscope: Configure both local MEmu instances for Fiddler Classic HTTP/HTTPS capture, maintain reboot recovery, and distin\r\nguish direct IM WebSocket traffic from observed Fiddler frames.\r\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents; reuse_rule=local executable paths, ADB serials, certificates, UI state, and N\r\nAT/host routing are machine/session-specific; do not call WebSocket capture complete without a fresh `101 Switching Pro\r\ntocols` session and frames.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Configure Fiddler Classic and MEmu proxy/HTTPS capture\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\D\r\nocuments, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9eb\r\ne-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: Fi\r\nddler Classic on 8866 and both VM HTTP/HTTPS proxy paths verified)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Fiddler Classic, Fiddler Everywhere, MEmu, adb.exe, memuc.exe, 127.0.0.1:21503, 127.0.0.1:21513, 10.0.2.2:8866, 26995\r\n3fb.0, AllowRemote, CaptureCONNECT\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Use a narrow host allowlist and reversible proxy on/off workflow\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\D\r\nocuments, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9eb\r\ne-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: Cu\r\nstomRules allowlist and direct-connect recovery verified)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- CustomRules.js, OnBeforeRequest, ui-hide, youpu, youpucq, youpuzg, 10.168.1.232, 10.168.1.233, settings delete global\r\n http_proxy, direct 200, Live Traffic, Inspectors, WebSocket, Messages\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Diagnose direct IM WebSocket bypass and restore HTTPS capture after emulator reboot\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\D\r\nocuments, rollout_path=\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\29\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9eb\r\ne-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, mixed: dire\r\nct-connection diagnosis and certificate-loss repair confirmed; unread-count payload not extracted)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 10.0.2.2:12728, x-overridehost, 101 Switching Protocols, uni.UNI8C317FA.youpu, proxy:000, cert-missing, curl: (60), 2\r\n69953fb.0, setup_cert_bindmount.sh, fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd, %%{http_code}, toybox nc -w\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when capture was too broad, the user said \"不要全部都抓，只抓ws和yopu相关的请求\", then added `10.168.1.232` and `.233\r\n` -> default to the narrow youpu/LAN allowlist and include every named host. [Task 2]\r\n- \"代理关了我的模拟器正常访问也得恢复\" -> proxy workflows must be reversible: verify direct access after disable and re\r\nstore proxy, certificate, and 200 validation when re-enabling. [Task 2]\r\n- when asking to look in WebSocket for login unread counts, the user expects inspection of actual payloads, not a reque\r\nst to paste messages. [Task 3]\r\n- repeated \"代理又坏了\" / \"抓不到了\" after restarts -> run the one-click repair, report VM0/VM1 `200`, and point to the\r\n self-service script; a startup scheduled task was offered but not adopted. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- The final working capture tool is Fiddler Classic on `::8866`; check `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 8866 -State Lis\r\nten`. Its `HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Fiddler2` settings are `ListenPort`=0x22a2, `AllowRemote`=True, and `CaptureCONNECT`\r\n=True. MEmu ADB is `D:\\soft\\Microvirt\\MEmu\\adb.exe`; VM0=`127.0.0.1:21503`, VM1=`127.0.0.1:21513`, and host loopback is\r\n `10.0.2.2`. [Task 1]\r\n- Set each proxy with `adb -s <serial> shell settings put global http_proxy 10.0.2.2:8866`; use device curl through `-x\r\n 10.0.2.2:8866` and expect 200. `memuc.exe listvms` identifies index 0/1; install the CA with `setup_cert_bindmount.sh`\r\n at `/system/etc/security/cacerts/269953fb.0`. [Task 1]\r\n- Related skill: skills/memu-fiddler-proxy-repair/SKILL.md.\r\n- The Fiddler display filter is `C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents\\Fiddler2\\Scripts\\CustomRules.js` `OnBeforeRequest`: use `ui-h\r\nide` unless the host includes `youpu`, `youpucq`, `youpuzg`, `10.168.1.232`, or `10.168.1.233`. Restart/reload Fiddler \r\nafter changes. Disable with `settings delete global http_proxy` and verify direct curl 200. [Task 2]\r\n- WebSocket frames, when routed through Fiddler, are in Live Traffic: select the `wss://`/`101` handshake, then `Inspec\r\ntors → WebSocket → Messages`. The app's IM connection to `10.0.2.2:12728` bypassed the 8866 system proxy; no unread-cou\r\nnt frame was captured. [Task 3]\r\n- Reboot restores MEmu `/system`, losing `/system/etc/security/cacerts/269953fb.0`: `proxy:000`, direct 200, `cert-miss\r\ning`, and curl (60) mean rerun `setup_cert_bindmount.sh`, reset proxy, then expect proxy curl 200. `C:\\Users\\79873\\Docu\r\nments\\fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd` is the canonical repair copy; a Desktop copy may be moved or renamed. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not recursively scan the whole disk for Fiddler logs/certs; start at `C:\\Users\\79873\\Documents\\Fiddler2` and `C:\\U\r\nsers\\79873\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\Fiddler`. `Fiddler Everywhere` winget downloads can hang; if needed, stop only the st\r\nuck winget and resume with `curl.exe -L --continue-at -` plus SHA256, but do not mistake it for the final working captu\r\nre tool. [Task 1]\r\n- Mixed PowerShell/adb/shell quoting breaks `%{http_code}` and nested braces; wrap the remote command in double quotes \r\nfrom PowerShell. `toybox nc -z` is unsupported; use `echo | toybox nc -w 3 host port`. Keep `CustomRules.js` minimal: a\r\n compile error silently disables all rules. [Task 2][Task 3]\r\n- Do not claim WebSocket capture from a listener or long TCP connection: require fresh `101 Switching Protocols` plus f\r\nrames. In the CMD repair script do not put `<-` in echo text because CMD treats `<` as redirection; invoke `cmd /c '...\r\n\\fix_fiddler_proxy.cmd'` without `< nul` from PowerShell. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IMServiceImpl benchmark bypass and Locust single-chat testing\r\nscope: Plan or implement a reproducible single-chat benchmark that retains the formal IM send path and MySQL persistenc\r\ne while suppressing Redis/Feign only within the controlled send branch.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=checkout-specific call-chain/line fa\r\ncts and partial design evidence; do not claim throughput, P99, or capacity until a real target-server run validates the\r\n counters and recipient delivery.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Retain the formal IMHandler → IMServiceImpl send path for benchmarking\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspa\r\nce\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25\r\nT13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c0\r\n3-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: redesign/analysis completed; no target-server benchmark result)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- IMHandler.handleSingleChat, IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage, BenchmarkMessagePath, Redis, Feign, MySQL, checkIdempote\r\nnt, deliverMessageToUser, CallerRunsPolicy\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Evaluate and redesign Locust single-chat testing\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-25T05-44-12-8wAs-imserviceimpl_locust_single_chat_benchmark_redesign.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspa\r\nce\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\25\\rollout-2026-07-25\r\nT13-44-12-019f97cd-768a-7c03-9d9c-1b73fce49b04.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-25T08:55:16+00:00, thread_id=019f97cd-768a-7c0\r\n3-9d9c-1b73fce49b04, partial: current script assessed; strict end-to-end redesign remains pending)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Locust, locustfile_single.py, users_*.json, WebSocket, cmd=1, cmd=5, cmd=27, fixed-pairing, success=false, result-500\r\n.html\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when performance work begins, the user asked “先给出方案 md” -> inspect code facts and provide a reviewable plan befo\r\nre modifying business code or running a load test. [Task 1]\r\n- when the first benchmark bypassed the business service, the user corrected: “为什么不去 imserviceImpl 实现类中把第三\r\n方调用来源禁用掉呢” -> benchmark the formal `IMHandler → IMServiceImpl` send path; bare Netty/in-memory Channel is only\r\n a secondary baseline. [Task 1]\r\n- the user said “只要保证在发送消息的时候目前不走 Redis、不调 Feign 就行” and “落库保留” -> constrain bypasses to send-\r\nstage Redis/Feign; retain MySQL message persistence/conversation update and keep any no-DB run as a separately labelled\r\n baseline. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user said “我先测单聊” and asked how the script works -> start with standalone, reproducible single-chat Loc\r\nust instructions and clearly distinguish the load-generator host from the target IM service. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- Formal single-chat entry: `IMHandler.handleSingleChat` → `IMServiceImpl.sendSingleMessage`; group entry: `handleGroup\r\nChat` → `sendGroupMessage`. The current send path also contains idempotency Redis, sender-profile cache, authorization \r\nthrough `RelationAuthorizationSnapshotReader` or `SendPrecheckFeignClient`, Redis routing/MQ/offline delivery, conversa\r\ntion cache, stranger limits, and moderation. [Task 1]\r\n- A valid persistence-retaining benchmark keeps message object/ID construction, MySQL or sharded write, and formal resp\r\nonse; it bypasses only the controlled Redis/Feign/cache/authorization/routing/remote-MQ/offline-push/unread/conversatio\r\nn-cache/moderation side paths, with local online Channel delivery. Verify branch hit count, MySQL writes, local deliver\r\nies, and Redis/Feign/MQ/offline call counters all together. [Task 1]\r\n- Group benchmark recipient lists originate from Redis authorization snapshots or Feign `getSendAuthorizationSnapshot`;\r\n if that source is bypassed, load a fixed local member snapshot rather than merely removing authorization. [Task 1]\r\n- `locustfile_single.py` loads `users_*.json`, opens formal WebSockets, logs in with `cmd=1`, sends single chat with `c\r\nmd=5`, and keeps heartbeat/reconnect behavior. Run `locust -f locustfile_single.py --web-host 0.0.0.0 --web-port 8090`;\r\n a headless example is `locust -f locustfile_single.py --headless -u 500 -r 50 --run-time 10m --html result-500.html`. \r\n[Task 2]\r\n- Current script is not a strict capacity test: it selects among 100 ring targets with 40/40/20 activity waits and only\r\n observes sender response. Use fixed pairs, explicit send rate, pre-exported JSON data, receiver `cmd=27` accounting, a\r\nnd loss/duplicate/out-of-order metrics for comparable 500/800/1000/2000/5000-user runs. [Task 2]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- `BenchmarkMessagePath` measured only Netty plus an in-memory Channel because it bypassed `IMServiceImpl`; first lock \r\ndown which layer is being measured, then implement a controlled branch in that layer. [Task 1]\r\n- Commenting a stranger-rate-limit step does not remove all external calls. Do not use `ss` alone as proof: instrument \r\ncode-level counters/logs and obtain target-service evidence. Static review cannot establish P99 or capacity. [Task 1]\r\n- Treat `resp.success=false` as a Locust failure and verify receiver `cmd=27`; sender-only acknowledgements otherwise o\r\nverstate delivery success. Do not embed credentials or query CRM/MySQL during the send window; prepare JSON beforehand.\r\n [Task 2]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM WebSocket EventLoop blocking audit\r\nscope: Read-only, source-backed review of whether IM WebSocket commands synchronously block the Netty EventLoop; use be\r\nfore planning performance remediation.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=the static call-chain finding is che\r\nckout-specific; recheck runtime instrumentation before quantifying latency or declaring production impact.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Audit IM WebSocket EventLoop blocking chain\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-24T09-20-52-ucN3-im_websocket_eventloop_blocking_audit.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkS\r\npace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\24\\rollout-2026-07-24T17-20-52-019f\r\n936d-752b-7f81-8856-55d5b5dc7601.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-24T09:23:38+00:00, thread_id=019f936d-752b-7f81-8856-55d5b5d\r\nc7601, success: source review confirmed synchronous blocking paths; no code changed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Netty, EventLoop, WebSocket, IMHandler, CommandDispatcher, ConversationServiceImpl, ConnectionManagerImpl, IMServiceI\r\nmpl, Redisson, Feign, CompletableFuture.get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS), CallerRunsPolicy\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user asked “目前代码的链路存在这个问题吗” and supplied a chain diagram -> give a definite, source-backed con\r\nclusion first; distinguish confirmed blocking from runtime-only impact. [Task 1]\r\n- when the request is an architecture/performance audit -> keep it read-only unless implementation is explicitly author\r\nized; first locate and attribute the chain, then propose remediation separately. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- `CommandDispatcher.dispatch()` is called from `IMHandler.channelRead0()` and directly invokes login, chat, read-ack, \r\nrevoke, reconnect, and call handlers; no business-executor handoff was found before these calls. [Task 1]\r\n- The login path synchronously does JWT validation, Redis route refresh, Redisson connection/cache work, DB conversatio\r\nn lookup, Feign user/group lookup, and offline-message DB read/delete plus Redis counter update. `ConversationServiceIm\r\npl.getRecentConversationList()` waits with `CompletableFuture.allOf(...).get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS)` and reads Redis per \r\nconversation. [Task 1]\r\n- `ConnectionManagerImpl` uses synchronous Redisson bucket reads/writes; per-conversation cache updates add linear Redi\r\ns round trips. Single/group send handlers directly invoke transactional `sendSingleMessage` / `sendGroupMessage`, inclu\r\nding Redis, database, and in some modes synchronous Feign authorization. [Task 1]\r\n- `ModerationQueueConfig.groupInfoQueryExecutor` uses `CallerRunsPolicy`; saturation can run blocking Feign work on the\r\n submitting EventLoop. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Static review did not run a benchmark, slow-dependency injection, or EventLoop metrics; do not quantify production P9\r\n9 impact from this evidence alone. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not async-wrap only one Feign call. Move the complete business command to a bounded business executor with fast re\r\njection/degradation, avoid `CallerRunsPolicy` fallback to EventLoop, and add EventLoop pending-task, command-duration, \r\ndependency-P99, and rejection metrics. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM relation separation, Redis-only cutover, and warmup scheduling\r\nscope: Keep relations authoritative in CRM Account, plan a fail-closed Redis-only authorization cutover, and stagger re\r\npair warmups; the rollout is design/acceptance evidence, not production validation.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck branch `dev-imtest`, Account\r\n/IM contracts, Redis state, and runtime topology; test/compile evidence does not replace middleware and real-client acc\r\neptance.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Design and review friend/group relation separation implementation and acceptance plan\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wo\r\nrkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07\r\n-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-\r\n7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: design review passed; real-environment acceptance not run)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- TB_FRIEND_RELATION, TB_GROUP_INFO, TB_GROUP_USER_RELATION, yopu-crm-account, SocialInternalFeignClient, fail-closed, \r\ngroupMemberCheck, Outbox, P0/P1/P2\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Plan direct Redis-only authorization cutover\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wo\r\nrkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07\r\n-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-\r\n7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: direct cutover procedure designed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- yopu.im.auth.running-mode=redis_only, TB_RELATION_CACHE_INVALIDATION_OUTBOX, /user/internal/job/im-auth-warmup/users,\r\n failedCount=0, yopu:im:warmup:failed:*, feign rollback\r\n\r\n## Task 3: Stagger the five Redis warmup jobs\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-18T03-10-12-ETuk-im_relation_separation_redis_only_pressure_test_and_cron.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\wo\r\nrkspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07\r\n-18T11-10-17-019f7333-f282-7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-03T12:11:48+00:00, thread_id=019f7333-f282-\r\n7d91-b7eb-26dbe20cc7f4, success: warmup schedule designed)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- Quartz CRON, 0 7/30 * * * ?, group-profiles, friend-views, group-member-views, after-commit, Outbox, skipped\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user requested “可落地的实施测试验收方案 md，然后评审，评审不过的话需要修改，直到评审通过” -> verify current\r\n code facts first, then provide boundaries, P0/P1/P2 tests, release gates, rollback, and iterative review. [Task 1]\r\n- for this relation plan, “保留公开接口、不迁移数据、不新建关系微服务” -> keep the minimal-risk CRM internal-domain bou\r\nndary. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- `yopu-crm-account` is authoritative for `TB_FRIEND_RELATION`, `TB_GROUP_INFO`, and `TB_GROUP_USER_RELATION`; IM reads\r\n the minimum relation data through internal Feign and must not write relation tables, duplicate relation data, migrate \r\ndata, or change public `/user/social/**` APIs. Authorization is fail-closed; on group dissolution, clear every `groupMe\r\nmberCheck(userId:groupId)`, not only the member-list cache. [Task 1]\r\n- Even when bypassing SHADOW, deploy Account and relation/Outbox DDL, validate Outbox, run all five warmups and samples\r\n (`skipped=false`, `failedCount=0`, `yopu:im:warmup:failed:*` empty), then switch every IM node to `yopu.im.auth.runnin\r\ng-mode=redis_only`. Roll back only to `feign` with a rolling IM restart; retain Redis, Outbox, and DDL. [Task 2]\r\n- Stagger the five repair jobs every 30 minutes: users `0 7/30 * * * ?`, groups `0 11/30 * * * ?`, group profiles `0 15\r\n/30 * * * ?`, friend views `0 19/30 * * * ?`, and group-member views `0 23/30 * * * ?`. Correctness comes from after-co\r\nmmit + Outbox; warmup is only repair/coverage scanning. If jobs overrun or often skip, investigate duration, failed set\r\ns, and MySQL/Redis load before moving to hourly staggering. [Task 3]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Markdown trailing double spaces break `git diff --check`; PowerShell Chinese-path/PPT handling needs `Path.glob('*.pp\r\ntx')`, `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8`, and `$doc = '...'` (not `a='...'`). Static review and documentation cannot replace Red\r\nis, RabbitMQ, Nacos, dual-node, and real-App acceptance. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not enable `redis_only` before warmup/sample evidence: a missing snapshot must deny authorization, not silently fa\r\nll back to Feign. Do not shorten an overrunning warmup cycle; diagnose load first. [Task 2][Task 3]\r\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM offline delivery, JPush environment isolation, and horizontal-scale safety\r\nscope: Audit, refactor, validate, and deploy Yopu IM online/offline delivery, JPush, RabbitMQ, DB migration, and Dev/pr\r\noduction push isolation.\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=use for this checkout's yopu-im arch\r\nitecture; production claims require live Nacos, RabbitMQ, DB, and client verification.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: Audit IM offline delivery, add a business-level offline-Push switch, and assess Dev/production JPush isolati\r\non\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-16T06-33-52-OCWh-im_offline_push_jpush_environment_isolation.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQia\r\nnWorkSpace\\youpu\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\07\\16\\rollout-2026-07-16T14-33-5\r\n4-019f69a1-b1d8-7a71-9ee3-ffa18e849f35.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-01T02:50:13+00:00, thread_id=019f69a1-b1d8-7a71-9ee3-f\r\nfa18e849f35, git_branch=dev-imtest, success: code audit and focused tests; live Nacos/device isolation remains unverifi\r\ned)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- offline-push, JPush, push.jiguang.enabled, im.offline-push.enabled, im.offline-push.cleanup-enabled, Registration ID,\r\n AppKey, Nacos, Redis, RabbitMQ, WebSocket, heartbeat, OfflinePushDispatcher, OfflinePushTaskAdmissionService, 1011\r\n\r\n## User preferences\r\n\r\n- when the user challenged the meaning of `push.jiguang.enabled: false` -> inspect the exact code path controlled by th\r\ne existing configuration before proposing another switch. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user requested a business-level total switch and asked whether switches should be merged -> preserve distinc\r\nt business, provider, and cleanup responsibilities rather than conflating them. [Task 1]\r\n- when the user asked to leave unrelated workspace changes untouched -> restrict edits to the named OfflinePush propert\r\nies, admission, dispatcher, config, and tests. [Task 1]\r\n- when assessing whether a Dev package can receive production Push -> verify runtime Nacos namespace/config, client App\r\nKey/package name, binding endpoint, and Redis isolation; source YAML alone is insufficient. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n## Reusable knowledge\r\n\r\n- `IMServiceImpl.deliverMessageToUser()` checks active local Netty channels, Redis multi-client routes, then remote MQ \r\nbefore offline persistence. Offline Push is separate: admission/persistence -> `OfflinePushDispatcher` -> direct/group \r\nRabbitMQ queues -> `OfflinePushTaskConsumer` -> `triggerOfflinePush()` -> `PushService`. [Task 1]\r\n- `push.jiguang.enabled` controls JPush SDK/provider bean creation via `PushAutoConfiguration`; it blocks JPush calls b\r\nut does not itself stop offline-message persistence or task creation. `im.offline-push.enabled` is the business switch:\r\n it blocks new task admission and real-time MQ dispatch, and makes claimed old tasks `SKIPPED` without calling JPush. N\r\normal WebSocket delivery and offline-message persistence remain enabled. [Task 1]\r\n- Keep `push.jiguang.enabled` as provider-level safety control and `im.offline-push.cleanup-enabled` as historical-task\r\n cleanup control; do not merge them into one ambiguous switch. [Task 1]\r\n- Device bindings are Redis keys `push:device:user:{userId}` and `push:device:reg:{registrationId}` with a 90-day TTL. \r\nAn accepted JPush API request is not device delivery; use delivery acknowledgement, device logs, and `msg_id + registra\r\ntion_id` to verify. `1011` means no valid Push target; a single-device request can clean its invalid binding, but bulk \r\nrequests cannot identify it precisely. [Task 1]\r\n- Different dev/prod source AppKey fingerprints reduce accidental cross-delivery, but Nacos can override runtime config\r\nuration. A real cross-environment proof requires uninstall-prod -> install-dev -> bind/login -> send from production, p\r\nlus Nacos, AppKey/package, binding endpoint, and Redis checks. [Task 1]\r\n- For Pre cleanup, remove both the `push:device:user:{userId}` Hash field and matching `push:device:reg:{registrationId\r\n}` reverse key; a full cleanup must use batched Redis `SCAN`, never `KEYS`, after Pre offline Push is disabled. [Task 1\r\n]\r\n\r\n## Failures and how to do differently\r\n\r\n- Do not stop `im-core` or ordinary message MQ consumers to disable offline Push; that can affect normal chat delivery.\r\n `@RefreshScope` does not prove all listener concurrency/config refreshes take effect: verify Nacos refresh, new-task c\r\nounts, MQ publishes, and JPush logs during rollout. [Task 1]\r\n- Do not infer production/device behavior from YAML or treat JPush API acceptance as delivery. Low-activity/terminated \r\nAndroid delivery also depends on OEM channels and `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`; iOS must match the APNs production/development \r\nenvironment. [Task 1]\r\n- Focused validation was `mvn -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am \"-Dtest=OfflinePushTaskAdmissionServiceTest,OfflinePushDispa\r\ntcherTest,OfflineMessagePersistenceServiceImplTest\" \"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\" test`: 12 tests, 0 failur\r\nes/errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`. This is not live Nacos/RabbitMQ/device acceptance. [Task 1]\r\n\r\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / storyboard production and asset governance\r\nscope: 伪纪录片图文生产编排、锁定资产、storyboard-first 文档、提示词模板合规和浏览器下载约束。\r\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\workspace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat; reuse_rule=follow current authority docs and inspect\r\n Git/untracked assets first.\r\n\r\n## Task 1: 05c asset lock, README V1.1 synchronization, and template-compliant reference-image regeneration\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-12T05-15-29-avoE-aigc_dali_cat_05c_asset_lock_doc_sync_imagegen_502.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspac\r\ne\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-08-12T13-15-3\r\n1-019ff465-a4eb-79e1-94cf-93fa34fe58e4.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-12T07:27:03+00:00, thread_id=019ff465-a4eb-79e1-94cf-9\r\n3fa34fe58e4, partial: four references regenerated; vertical-slit entity remains pending)\r\n\r\n### keywords\r\n\r\n- 05c, 神尸地图, assets/README.md, V1.1, 图03, 图08, 图11, 图14, 图16, 图21, 现实侵入式伪纪录片_通用提示词模板_V1.0.md,\r\n 2034, imagegen 502, 透明竖缝, 杨戬三眼脸\r\n\r\n## Task 2: Repair masters, lock S00, and establish EP001 storyboard-first workflow\r\n\r\n### rollout_summary_files\r\n\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-11T07-53-25-BHXE-project_state_check_next_step_v2_masters_repair_first.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\works\r\npace\\YeQianWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-11T15-5\r\n3-27-019f502a-bcc4-7223-9e0f-c86f7cb842c6.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-11T07:54:16+00:00, thread_id=019f502a-bcc4-7223-9e0\r\nf-c86f7cb842c6)\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-11T16-19-44-cvNy-download_s00_assets_browser_url_uncertain.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQianW\r\norkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-12T00-19-49-019f51f\r\na-4724-7791-8ba7-34a31d3dfb2c.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-11T16:20:28+00:00, thread_id=019f51fa-4724-7791-8ba7-34a31d3dfb\r\n2c)\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-11T16-28-54-n8lo-s00_lockboard_move_update_first_episode_push.md (cwd=\\\\?\\D:\\workspace\\YeQi\r\nanWorkSpace\\yeqian\\aigc-dali-cat, rollout_path=C:\\Users\\79873\\.codex\\archived_sessions\\rollout-2026-07-12T00-28-59-019f\r\n5202-a9cf-74b3-a64e-3e00c135d746.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-11T16:49:38+00:00, thread_id=019f5202-a9cf-74b3-a64e-3e00c13\r\n5d746)\r\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-12T01-53-35-zfrH-storyboard