d authority in this order: `START_HERE.md` → `SKILL.md` → `AGENTS.md` → `standards/制作规范_正式版.md` → active `s\\r\\ntandards/AUTHORITY_INDEX.json` → episode docs → `meta/episode-state.json`. Use `python episodes/_system/preproduction_h\\r\\nandoff.py verify <episode_dir>` as the authority check, not a hand-rolled SHA loop; on success `activate` changes only \\r\\nthe active mode to `image_continue` and leaves `runtime-request.json` immutable. [Task 1]\\r\\n- `stable_preproduction_subset` includes Story plus `visual.environment_contract`/`frame_directives`/`calibration`. A l\\r\\nater legal Visual Lock calibration write can therefore cause `HANDOFF_SHA_MISMATCH:meta/story-gates.json#stable_preprod\\r\\nuction_subset`; it is a signature-boundary conflict, not proof Story was rewritten. Stop and decide whether to exclude \\r\\nruntime fields or rebuild the handoff legitimately; never silently recreate the signature. [Task 1][Task 4]\\r\\n- The ledger state machine is `PENDING` through `NEEDS_USER` and `PASSED`/`LOCKED`; a second hard failure after one con\\r\\ntent repair becomes `NEEDS_USER`. `accept-user-exception-candidate` is deliberately narrow: accept only a `NEEDS_USER` \\r\\ncurrent candidate whose SHA matches the Frame Contract/Visual profile, record the user approval text and `direct_user_r\\r\\neview_exception_acceptance`, then set `PASSED`. Do not hand-edit JSON to bypass the gate. [Task 2]\\r\\n- `visual_lock_v21.bind-from-queue` must bind all required images. A `scout_repair` candidate is eligible only when the\\r\\n ledger is PASSED, lineage SHA matches the current candidate, and the direct-acceptance audit matches. `INPUT_IMAGES_UN\\r\\nAVAILABLE` is evidence absence, not content failure; preserve it and use `restore-evidence-gap-review` only for the def\\r\\nined mis-downgrade case. [Task 2][Task 3]\\r\\n- Visual Lock V2.1 accepts policy exactly `four_admission_v21`; `four_admission_v21_1_plus_3` is not recognized. The fo\\r\\nur roles are ordinary baseline → worst capture condition → first major anomaly → high-impact admission; this episode bo\\r\\nund 01/05/08/17, but `validate_episode.py`/`machine_gate.py`/`evidence_gate.py` remain the sole legal progression gates\\r\\n. [Task 2]\\r\\n- Windows critic shield: pass Chinese prompt text as UTF-8 bytes rather than `text=True`; copy Chinese-path images to A\\r\\nSCII temporary attachments before `-i`; clean up the temporary directory. `CreateProcessWithLogonW failed: 1385` means \\r\\nthe worker cannot inspect pixels, so record `INPUT_IMAGES_UNAVAILABLE` and do not claim Visual Lock pass. [Task 3]\\r\\n- Progress reports belong in `episodes/<episode>/meta/`, not frozen `story/`. Separate machine-stage, candidate-frame, \\r\\nPASSED-frame, approved-frame, and weighted-work-package percentages rather than calling generated files completed produ\\r\\nction. [Task 4]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- Symptom: `visual_lock_v21.py show-plan` says Visual Lock is not required for an episode expected to be V2.1. Cause: t\\r\\nhe policy spelling is unsupported. Fix: search templates, gates, and the script's `required()` check before changing st\\r\\nate; use the exact recognized policy. [Task 2]\\r\\n- Symptom: `Reading prompt from stdin... input is not valid UTF-8` or Chinese image attachments cannot load. Cause: Win\\r\\ndows code page and non-ASCII path handling. Fix: byte stdin plus ASCII temporary copies. A missing `import tempfile` ca\\r\\nuses `NameError`; rerun the critic after the import and preserve its actual result. [Task 3]\\r\\n- Symptom: critic returns `INPUT_IMAGES_UNAVAILABLE`. Cause: Windows sandbox worker startup fails with `CreateProcessWi\\r\\nthLogonW failed: 1385`, not an image-content rejection. Fix: leave the episode at the evidence gate; do not downgrade f\\r\\nrames to content failure or advance `VISUAL_CALIBRATED`. [Task 3]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / Codex image-generation channel and Story OS worker diagnost