 snapshot, hard-delete, six-type collection flow. Preserve old interfaces/tables and build an indep\\r\\nendent collection chain. [Task 1]\\r\\n- `TB_MESSAGE_0~31` routes by `Math.floorMod(SHARD_UID,32)`, so `msgId` alone cannot locate a row. Reuse existing hot/c\\r\\nold message-query routing rather than add a locator table or modify send flow. Supported types are `1,2,3,4,5,10`; unsu\\r\\npported types return `2012003`. [Task 1]\\r\\n- New contract: `POST /v1/im/message/collect {sourceMsgId}` accepts `PROCESSING`; `GET .../list` shows READY only; `DEL\\r\\nETE .../{collectId}` hard-deletes in the current user scope and is idempotent. Media-copy disabled yields `2012011`. [T\\r\\nask 1]\\r\\n- `GET /v1/im/message/collect/list` accepts `pageNum`/`pageSize` (default 20, max 50), returns `records/size/current/ha\\r\\nsMore`, and orders READY records by `collectedAt DESC, id DESC`. Gateway testing uses `http://10.168.1.233:9001` with J\\r\\nWT; direct `8085` requires `X-User-Id`. [Task 1]\\r\\n- `im.collection` defaults are 1000 records/user, 2GB logical bytes/user, and 200MB/single file. `TB_MESSAGE_COLLECTION\\r\\n_QUOTA_{0..31}` atomically reserves count/bytes, converts reserve to used on success, releases on failure/cancel/delete\\r\\n; text/location uses `mediaBytes=0`. Codes: `2012006` count, `2012007` bytes, `2012008` file too large, `2012012` physi\\r\\ncal capacity. [Task 1]\\r\\n- PRD status: 2GB, 1000 records/text-no-bytes, 200MB, and full-space error are implemented (P0-14 quota checks passed w\\r\\nithout rejected records being stored). Image ≤1600px/video 720p/voice-original are not implemented: current `snapshotPr\\r\\nofile=origin` requires file-service OSS expansion and dev end-to-end integration. `physical-warn-ratio=0.8` is only a c\\r\\nonfiguration placeholder; current code logs physical bytes every 10 minutes. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Gateway IM routes in `yopu-gateway/.../application.yaml`, `application-test.yaml`, and `application-prod.yaml` must u\\r\\nse `StripPrefix=0`: IM controllers include `/v1/im`, whereas `/v1/user/**` correctly remains `StripPrefix=1` because it\\r\\ns controller is `/user/...`. Fix committed as `baac8443f` / merged `973146962`; running gateway must restart. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Use `UK_USER_SOURCE_MSG(USER_ID,SOURCE_MSG_ID)`, list index `(USER_ID,COLLECTED_AT DESC,ID DESC)`, stable media finge\\r\\nrprint reuse, separate bounded Worker with `AbortPolicy`, collection DLQ `yopu.im.collection.task.dlq`, and default-off\\r\\n `im.collection.enabled` / `im.collection.media-copy-enabled` gates. [Task 1]\\r\\n- 28 collection tests, DDL/entity/XML consistency checks, and `git diff --check` passed; package used `mvn clean packag\\r\\ne -pl yopu-im/yopu-im-core -am -Dmaven.test.skip=true` because five unrelated legacy tests failed compilation. Formal P\\r\\n0 remains blocked until DBA runs DDL, `10.168.1.233:3306` is reachable, file service provides copy/signing, six samples\\r\\n are finalized, and integration/load runs complete. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Migration implementation: `im.collection.enabled=true`, retain `consumer-enabled=true`, and keep `media-copy-enabled=\\r\\nfalse` until the file-service contract exists. Mark `GroupMsgCollectController` / service and its OpenAPI operations de\\r\\nprecated, and point API docs to `消息收藏-服务端API契约.md`. Commits recorded: `749a97df7`, `70e199f26`. [Task 2]\\r\\n- `CollectionSnapshotBuilder.looksLikeUrl` must treat a relative objectKey containing `/` plus a file extension as a me\\r\\ndia reference; otherwise real IM media tasks can empty-spin SUCCESS with no `mediaList`. `mediaMessageExtractsRelativeO\\r\\nbjectKey` covers this. [Task 2]\\r\\n- IM dev is read/write split: writes on `10.168.1.233`, reads on `10.168.1.232`. `TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX_*` has no `CREA\\r\\nTE_TIME` or `UPDATE_TIME`; remove `UPDATE_TIME = NOW()` from `batchUpsertSessionIndex` rather than searching for a miss\\r\\ning migration. Fix committed as `212d2773e` (relative objectKey) and `0f3f63a94` (UPDATE_TIME). [Task 2]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- Never use login success, sender stats, or MQ drain as capacity proof: require `cmd5=cmd6=cmd27=cmd7`, `ackPending=0`,\\r\\n and MQ/Outbox tail completion. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Delete/reconciliation can race Worker `PENDING->READY`: lock the current row with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`, then relea\\r\\nse quota based on latest state. Scan text/location timeouts (5s) separately from media (60s) so slow media does not sta\\r\\nrve recovery. [Task 1]\\r\\n- A `{\\\"code\\\":404,\\\"msg\\\":\\\"资源不存在\\\"}` response can be the downstream `GlobalExceptionHandler` (HTTP 200), not the gatew\\r\\nay itself. Grep `资源不存在`, then compare direct complete `/v1/im/...` to the same instance's stripped path; if only s\\r\\ntripped fails, align StripPrefix. Do not hide DB errors with `2>$null`; inspect `SHOW COLUMNS` and the read/write topol\\r\\nogy first. [Task 1][Task 2]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: Windows Clash Verge Rev proxy traffic and OpenCodex context replay diagnosis\\r\\nscope: Diagnose why Clash rule mode still consumes large VPN traffic, identify the actual source process, and apply the\\r\\n correct profile-rule or OpenCodex context-cap change.\\r\\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\Documents; reuse_rule=subscription/profile names, paths, ports, traffic totals, and acti\\r\\nve configuration are machine/time-specific; reuse the runtime-first diagnostic sequence and source-port process attribu\\r\\ntion.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 1: Diagnose rule-mode traffic and repair the bound subscription rules\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-09-38-JDVn-clash_opencodex_traffic_web_gpt_image_handoff_skill.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\7\\r\\n9873\\\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\08\\\\14\\\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-09-38-019ffe08-3347-7b\\r\\n52-8094-015eaf08d979.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T06:10:44+00:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\\r\\nss: live rule-mode attribution and traffic-control pivot established)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- Clash Verge Rev, verge-mihomo, 127.0.0.1:9097, mixed-port 7897, /configs, /rules, /connections, MATCH,节点选择, profi\\r\\nles.yaml, rUwK2myX1tfT.yaml, GEOSITE,cn, OpenNetMeter\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 2: Trace OpenCodex-to-ChatGPT uploads and lower replay context\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-09-38-JDVn-clash_opencodex_traffic_web_gpt_image_handoff_skill.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\7\\r\\n9873\\\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\08\\\\14\\\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-09-38-019ffe08-3347-7b\\r\\n52-8094-015eaf08d979.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T06:10:44+00:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\\r\\nss: replay mechanism, cap limits, and image-work offload established)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- OpenCodex, bun.exe, chatgpt.com, metadata.sourcePort, Get-NetTCPConnection, openai_base_url, 127.0.0.1:10100, context\\r\\nCapValue, providerContextCaps, usage.jsonl, expandPreviousResponseInput, previous_response_id\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 3: Move image generation to official web ChatGPT with a handoff skill\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-09-38-JDVn-clash_opencodex_traffic_web_gpt_image_handoff_skill.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\7\\r\\n9873\\\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\08\\\\14\\\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-09-38-019ffe08-3347-7b\\r\\n52-8094-015eaf08d979.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-19T06:10:44+00:00, thread_id=019ffe08-3347-7b52-8094-015eaf08d979, succe\\r\\nss: handoff skill, project rule, and vision-sidecar disablement applied)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- web-gpt-image-handoff, 官方网页ChatGPT, visionSidecar.enabled, AGENTS.md, image_gen, copy-ready handoff sheet, 10-per\\r\\n-batch\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 4: Diagnose OpenCodex 401 account-pool and recurring 400 errors\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-14T02-20-26-xprg-opencodex_bun_proxy_error_diagnostics_401_oom_tool_state.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Us\\r\\ners\\\\79873\\\\Documents, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\08\\\\14\\\\rollout-2026-08-14T10-20-26-019ffe12-16\\r\\n40-76a0-a32f-77d9a287cb76.jsonl, updated_at=2026-09-01T01:38:59+00:00, thread_id=019ffe12-1640-76a0-a32f-77d9a287cb76, \\r\\nsuccess: root causes separated and revalidated)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- CodexPoolAuthenticationError, 401 Unauthorized, chatgpt.com, wham/usage, usage.jsonl, service.log, Invalid JSON body,\\r\\n RangeError: Out of memory, Bun 1.3.14, Duplicate tool output for call_id, prompt_cache_retention, prompt_cache_options\\r\\n, Cloudflare challenge\\r\\n\\r\\n## User preferences\\r\\n\\r\\n- when the user says “我一直开的规则模式啊，你看看是不是配置有问题” -> do not start by blaming an accidental global-mod\\r\\ne switch; read live `/configs`, `/rules`, and the active profile binding before concluding. [Task 1]\\r\\n- when the user asks “怎么去APP界面里面查询” -> provide a self-recheck path as well as the diagnosis. [Task 1]\\r\\n- when the user says “做调整” / “帮我改了” after a diagnosed, reversible fix -> apply it and verify the runtime result \\r\\ninstead of stopping at advice. [Task 1][Task 2]\\r\\n- when the user says “后面出图我只想用网页版本的gpt，给我方案” and “把这个落成skill” -> for AIGC image generation/edits\\r\\n, produce copy-ready prompt handoff sheets for official web ChatGPT; do not initiate image tools, browser automation, o\\r\\nr bulk media upload through Codex/OpenCodex. [Task 3]\\r\\n- when troubleshooting this machine, the user asks in Chinese why 401 persists despite free quota -> answer in Chinese \\r\\nand distinguish credential state, ChatGPT reachability, and quota up front. [Task 4]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reusable knowledge\\r\\n\\r\\n- Start with Clash `GET /configs`, `/proxies`, `/connections`, `/version`, and `/rules` at `http://127.0.0.1:9097`. A t\\r\\nerminal `MATCH,节点选择` in rule mode sends all non-domestic/unmatched traffic to the proxy: “局部” is domestic/allowli\\r\\nst routing, not only explicitly named sites. Use `connections[].chains` to distinguish DIRECT from a node. [Task 1]\\r\\n- To change a subscription's rules, first locate the active profile in `profiles.yaml` and its `option.rules` binding. \\r\\nOn this machine the effective file is `profiles/rUwK2myX1tfT.yaml`; adding `DOMAIN-SUFFIX,deepseek.com,DIRECT` and `GEO\\r\\nSITE,cn,DIRECT` to its `prepend` then restarting `clash-verge.exe` put GeoSite cn into live `/rules`. Global `Merge.yam\\r\\nl`, profile Merge `prepend-rules`, and core-only restart did not reliably rebuild the runtime configuration. [Task 1]\\r\\n- OpenNetMeter requires admin installation and records Clash-forwarded connections as `verge-mihomo`; query its `OpenNe\\r\\ntMeter.sqlite` `ProcessDate` joins for daily per-process totals, then use Clash `/connections` plus `metadata.sourcePor\\r\\nt` -> `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort <port>` -> process lookup to identify the real client. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Codex is routed through OpenCodex by `openai_base_url = \\\"http://127.0.0.1:10100/v1\\\"`. OpenCodex expands `previous_res\\r\\nponse_id` into full local input (`expandPreviousResponseInput`); the ChatGPT backend rejects that continuation ID, so i\\r\\nt repeatedly uploads full history. `contextCapValue` and every `providerContextCaps` in `C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.opencodex\\\\conf\\r\\nig.json` cap replay tokens, not network bytes; lowering 950000 to 200000 reduced but did not eliminate traffic. [Task 2\\r\\n]\\r\\n- For high-frequency image/story work through OpenCodex, start a new Codex task after a completed storyboard/chapter an\\r\\nd send reference images only when needed; long repeated sessions replay text and visual context. Web ChatGPT does not h\\r\\nave the same client-side replay amplification because its history stays server-side. [Task 2]\\r\\n- The durable image-work path is three layers: project `AGENTS.md` rule, global `web-gpt-image-handoff` skill, and `vis\\r\\nionSidecar.enabled=false`. The handoff includes per-frame positive prompt, locks, negatives, filename, and 10-image acc\\r\\neptance checklist; user generates/downloads manually in web ChatGPT. [Task 3]\\r\\n- For this proxy, `C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.opencodex\\\\usage.jsonl` is the fast status/model ledger and `service.log` is the erro\\r\\nr root-cause source. A 401 `CodexPoolAuthenticationError` means OpenCodex selected no usable account; first run account\\r\\n-state/WHAM checks and probe `chatgpt.com` via Clash. An active free account with remaining quota still fails when reac\\r\\nhability is `000`; WHAM 200/401 shows the API is reachable. Invoke `ocx.ps1` through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionP\\r\\nolicy Bypass -File ...` if execution policy blocks the shim. [Task 4]\\r\\n- Here `Invalid JSON body` was Bun request decoding after `RangeError: Out of memory`, not user JSON. Grep `service.log\\r\\n` for `request body decode/parse failed|panic\\\\(|Bun has crashed`; a ~950k context cap and giant sessions drove Bun 1.3.\\r\\n14 crashes. Start a new session, lower context caps to roughly 128k-256k, restart/upgrade OpenCodex, then monitor RSS. \\r\\n[Task 4]\\r\\n- `Duplicate tool output for call_id` points to client/proxy replay of a damaged session: stop retrying it, use a new t\\r\\nask, then restart/upgrade only if new tasks fail. `prompt_cache_retention is not supported on this model` is an auto-in\\r\\njected deprecated parameter; do not add it manually—upgrade the client to use `prompt_cache_options.ttl`. A Cloudflare \\r\\nchallenge HTML/403 from the homepage reflects the exit IP, not account quota; switch node/use a real browser and test t\\r\\nhe actual WHAM endpoint. [Task 4]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- Editing global `Merge.yaml` and profile Merge before checking `profiles.yaml` wasted two attempts because neither fil\\r\\ne was compiled into live `/rules`; discover the bound custom-rule file first, then restart the Clash Verge application \\r\\nand verify `/rules`. [Task 1]\\r\\n- `verge-mihomo.exe -t -f clash-verge.yaml` can fail with `can't download MMDB: context deadline exceeded` when offline\\r\\n GeoIP/MMDB is absent; that does not prove a rule syntax failure when the running core already has the data. Validate l\\r\\nive `/rules` instead. [Task 1]\\r\\n- OpenNetMeter alone cannot distinguish direct from proxy traffic because it attributes both forwarded traffic to `verg\\r\\ne-mihomo`; do not stop at its process name—correlate the high-upload connection's source port and Clash chain. [Task 1]\\r\\n- A 200k replay cap is not a byte cap: multiple concurrent 200k+ context tasks can still consume GBs. For image/story r\\r\\nuns, switching the image step away from OpenCodex is the actual traffic-control pivot. [Task 2][Task 3]\\r\\n- Do not blame an expired subscription based only on `active_until`; this was initially wrong. Check `ocx account list \\r\\n--json --all` and live WHAM before attributing a 401 to account state. [Task 4]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: aigc-dali-cat / Douyin operations, subtitle review, topic research, and 05d regeneration\\r\\nscope: Browser-dependent Douyin metrics collection, subtitle QA, topic research boundaries, K1 comparison routing, and \\r\\nrelease-image validation for the story-production pipeline.\\r\\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\\\workspace\\\\YeQianWorkSpace\\\\yeqian\\\\aigc-dali-cat; reuse_rule=follow current `standards/制作规范_正式版\\r\\n.md` and episode evidence; browser-config state and individual assets are time-specific.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 1: Handle browser-blocked Douyin data collection and complete S1 subtitle review\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-12T05-59-04-OU27-douyin_data_