iness TPS separate. [Task 1]\\r\\n- when the user corrected the host roles: \\\"165 作为纯粹的压力机，47是IM服务器\\\" -> confirm host role and private address\\r\\n before attributing CPU, network, or JVM evidence. [Task 2]\\r\\n- when the user asked to analyze the bottleneck first and \\\"不要盲目加线程\\\" -> add segment evidence before changing pool\\r\\n sizes. [Task 2]\\r\\n- when load exceeds 500, the user specified \\\"165 as the primary pressure host, then 75, 89\\\" -> state host roles and spl\\r\\nit ownership explicitly rather than distributing users arbitrarily. [Task 4]\\r\\n- when the user asked \\\"修复，然后看看还存在啥问题\\\" -> after each repair, audit remaining reliability gaps and distingui\\r\\nsh verified fixes from unverified risks. [Task 5]\\r\\n- when optimizing IM performance, the user required latest analysis and real load-test evidence, and rejected treating \\r\\nfinal drain or historical cumulative metrics as a steady-business-window conclusion -> distinguish business-window delt\\r\\nas from drain state and static/code evidence. [Task 8]\\r\\n- when comparing branches, the user asked what is different and what can be learned for single chat -> separate product\\r\\nion governance, load-test-only logic, and production-safe reusable changes; return a priority-ordered landing list rath\\r\\ner than a diff dump. [Task 9]\\r\\n- when planning batch execution, the user explicitly said “优先调整批量执行并发，不增大队列” -> change only `executor-p\\r\\nool-size` through 8, 16, then only if needed 24/32; do not jump to 32. [Task 8]\\r\\n- when judging 2000 QPS, the user continued to require strict protocol closure and actual evidence rather than login su\\r\\nccess or sender statistics -> require `cmd5=cmd6=cmd27=cmd7=planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`,\\r\\n and MQ/Outbox drain before making a capacity claim. [Task 10]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reusable knowledge\\r\\n\\r\\n- Before a rerun, confirm the pre RabbitMQ backlog is cleared or record its baseline, then verify 47 health, the deploy\\r\\ned JMeter file, and current process configuration. Historical backlog-induced `cmd=27` delay is not a capacity result f\\r\\nor the new run. [Task 3]\\r\\n- `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous.jmx` uses one long-lived JDK 17 WebSocket per real user; users both send and receiv\\r\\ne, targets are mapped after login, and the final summary records cmd=5/6/27/7, QPS/TPS, P50/P95/P99, delivery/ACK rate,\\r\\n loss, duplicates, and ordering. `users.json` has only 500 valid users, so larger runs require more real credentials an\\r\\nd friend mappings. [Task 1]\\r\\n- The validated cross-host P0 used 165=`139.196.23.165`/`172.20.196.192` as the JMeter pressure host and 47=`47.116.106\\r\\n.227`/`172.20.196.193` as the IM server. With two users at one message/user/second for 30 seconds, `cmd=5/6/27/7=60/60/\\r\\n60/60`, delivery/ACK were 100%, and loss/duplicates/out-of-order were zero: P0 only, not a capacity result. [Task 2]\\r\\n- `SingleChatPerformanceObserver` localized the gap to business execution through local Netty push write: cmd=6 P50/P95\\r\\n/P99=`489/504/748ms`, cmd=27=`449/459/663ms`, queued-to-executing is near zero, pushWritten is about 441–452ms, and pus\\r\\nhWritten-to-ACK about 3–5ms. Add segmented timing across persistence, routing, MQ publish/confirm, MQ consumer, and pus\\r\\nh before altering fixed pool sizes; socket writes remain on the channel EventLoop. [Task 2]\\r\\n\\r\\n- For the 2000-user three-host run, shard 165=1200, 75=500, 89=300 without overlap and confirm each shard has local onl\\r\\nine-friend targets. `allLoginTimeoutMs` must exceed the login ramp; 240s ramp with a 180s gate timed out, while a 360s \\r\\ngate passed login. Capacity acceptance requires login, business, final protocol aggregate, and MQ/Outbox tail together.\\r\\n [Task 4]\\r\\n- The 2026-08-03 three-host result is not a capacity pass: `cmd5=60000`, `cmd6/cmd27=59998`, `cmd7=59786` (2 missing me\\r\\nssages and 212 ACK gap); MQ/Outbox tail was not verified. The 165-only run also cannot support a strict 2000 msg/s clai\\r\\nm because staggered login compressed send time (`cmd5=57172`, `cmd6/cmd27=57167`, `cmd7=57165`). Rework the JMX into a \\r\\ntwo-stage model with shared `businessStartAt` and a fixed 30s business window after all users log in. [Task 4]\\r\\n- `IMHandler.handleMessageDeliverAck()` had marked receipt without `MessageAckService.confirmAck(userId,msgId)`, leavin\\r\\ng Redis pending keys and enabling duplicate direct pushes. The repair calls `confirmAck` for `cmd=7`; `IMServiceImpl` a\\r\\nnd `MessageConsumer` register pending before WebSocket write and cancel it on write failure; retry exhaustion/offline d\\r\\nelivery uses idempotent `OfflineMessagePersistenceService.persist` before clearing pending/retry keys. `MessageAckServi\\r\\nce` defaults observed in source: pending TTL 300s, max retry 3, Redis-key scan retry. Package validation (`mvn -pl yopu\\r\\n-im/yopu-im-core -am package \\\"-Dmaven.test.skip=true\\\"`) and `git diff --check` passed. [Task 5]\\r\\n- The matrix script is `im_single_chat_duplex_continuous_codex.jmx`. A short-window result is acceptable only when logi\\r\\nn, business-send, final-summary, four-command closure, and MQ/Outbox tail all pass. `matrix-1500-rerun-20260803` met `1\\r\\n500/0` for main samples with MQ `ready/unack/consumers=0/0/8` and Outbox zero; retain the earlier 1000 login and 1500 b\\r\\nusiness failures as variability/reliability evidence. [Task 6]\\r\\n- `matrix-2000-20260803` used 2000 threads, 240s ramp, 30s business window, and 330s duration after zero MQ/Outbox gate\\r\\ns. Nineteen users did not reach a 180s login barrier; `IM_LOGIN_CONNECT 1981/0` was followed by `IM_BUSINESS_CONTINUOUS\\r\\n_SEND 1981/1981`. This is a load-generator/readiness failure, not a valid 2000-user IM-throughput result. [Task 6]\\r\\n- C0/C1 single-variable evidence identifies `TB_USER_SESSION_INDEX` UPSERT as the current 1000-QPS bottleneck: disablin\\r\\ng it changed cmd6 P50/P95 from 17.9s/39.4s to 69ms/108ms, restored about 999.8/s persistence, and reduced lock waits 99\\r\\n.7%. P1-A batch-local merge/sort by `(USER_ID, SESSION_ID)` reduces one-batch contention but is not cross-consumer key \\r\\nserialization. [Task 8]\\r\\n- P1-A is not accepted: business P50/P95 was 40/56ms but Outbox unapplied was 96,146 (53%); same-key cross-batch/cross-\\r\\nconsumer UPSERT contention remained. Use fixed-key partition serialization and bounded batching only after real P1-B lo\\r\\nad evidence. [Task 8]\\r\\n- Scheme B: `ChatDbBatchDispatcher` aggregates 50ms, groups `SHARD_UID % 32`, and defaults to an 8-thread per-shard exe\\r\\ncutor; `ChatDbBatchProperties.enabled=false`. `ChatDbBatchPersistService` writes messages and matching Outbox in one tr\\r\\nansaction, retries only routing/deadlock errors, then uses row-wise idempotent fallback. Watch `[IM-CHATDB-BATCH]` and \\r\\n`[IM-THREADPOOL]`; pre-production 96/128-thread settings do not validate production 24/48 with `chat-db=false`. [Task 8\\r\\n]\\r\\n- `dev-im-merge` is a production candidate baseline (thread/MQ isolation, bounded queues, `AbortPolicy`, optional CPU a\\r\\nffinity); `dev-imtest` is the stricter real-user JMeter/closed-loop observability system. Production-safe single-chat p\\r\\nriorities are: `RBatch` for login/heartbeat while preserving routing/online/TTL semantics, move heartbeat Redis work of\\r\\nf Netty workers and return explicit failure ACK on rejection, offline/DLQ fallback with `NACK(requeue=false)`, then min\\r\\nimize the persistence/session-index transaction. Async DB needs durable compensation and 500/1000-user A/B before enabl\\r\\nement; CPU affinity/pool expansion are later experiments. [Task 9]\\r\\n- Verified chain: Netty decode/auth -> `messageProcessor` authorization precheck -> `SingleChatPersistenceTask` on `cha\\r\\ntDbAsyncExecutor` / `im-asyncdb-` -> message main table plus session Outbox in the `saveSingleMessage` transaction -> l\\r\\nocal synchronous push or cross-node MQ (offline only when no online route) -> cmd6 ACK. The session index uses 16 seria\\r\\nl partitions, 150 records/50ms aggregation, ledger deduplication, batch upsert, and post-commit cache invalidation. Sou\\r\\nrce-default Outbox polling is 100ms but Nacos can override it at runtime. [Task 10]\\r\\n- The five-node 200 QPS x 120s run (23,994 messages) closed at aggregate 1000 QPS only; it cannot establish 2000 QPS or\\r\\n validate a high-single-host connection model. Use 1500 QPS x 180s for three all-zero rounds -> 2000 QPS x 180s -> 2000\\r\\n QPS x 10min for three all-zero rounds, with `CallerRuns=0`, stable P99, and no sustained MySQL/Redis/MQ saturation. [T\\r\\nask 10]\\r\\n- Prioritize bounded queues with fast rejection/explicit busy metrics over `CallerRunsPolicy`, restore transactional pe\\r\\nrsistent `(senderId, clientMsgId)` idempotency that returns the first `messageId`, then add segmented cmd6 metrics befo\\r\\nre tuning pools. Local synchronous push may reduce cmd27 but occupies `im-asyncdb-`; test the proposed independent boun\\r\\nded delivery executor with A/B evidence before claiming throughput gains. [Task 10]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- Do not run directly when queue status, 47 health, JMeter artifact, or process configuration is unknown; do not attrib\\r\\nute an old queue backlog to the new run's capacity. [Task 3]\\r\\n- `DuplexListener` cannot read outer JMeter `props`: `groovy.lang.MissingPropertyException: No such property: props for\\r\\n class: DuplexListener` -> pass command configuration through shared listener state. [Task 1]\\r\\n- A failed early smoke can be a script/runtime issue, not an IM performance result: inspect JTL `responseMessage` and `\\r\\nlistenerError` first. For restarts, verify actual PID, 8084/8085, health, and `/actuator/beans` wiring for `singleChatP\\r\\nerformanceObserver`, not only the JAR filename. [Task 2]\\r\\n- `--spring.cloud.nacos.enabled=false` does not reliably suppress Nacos ConfigData import; a known recovery path explic\\r\\nitly supplies `--spring.config.import=optional:file:/opt/yopu-apps/conf/application-pre.yaml`, then verifies service he\\r\\nalth. Monitor RSS, Direct Memory, GC, and OOM before high-connection tests on 47 because `-Xmx50g + MaxDirectMemorySize\\r\\n=10g` leaves little headroom on 64G. [Task 2]\\r\\n- Do not call a run passed solely because all users logged in or a sender-side total looks complete. Require `cmd5 == c\\r\\nmd6 == cmd27 == cmd7 == planned`, zero loss/duplicate/out-of-order, `ackPending=0`, and MQ/Outbox tail completion. [Tas\\r\\nk 4]\\r\\n- Do not claim the new ACK/offline tests passed: existing `IMServiceImplTest.java:[119,33]` and `[121,34]` fail test co\\r\\nmpilation because `isRetryableShardingRouteException(IllegalStateException)` is missing. Remaining risks: offline-persi\\r\\nstence failure retains only pending TTL, ACK misses are DEBUG-only, Redis full scans can cause retry bursts, and long J\\r\\nMeter runs do not reclaim `sent/byContent` maps. In PowerShell, quote whole Maven `-D` arguments. [Task 5]\\r\\n- When a 2000 run has incomplete login at the barrier, do not call the downstream business errors an IM capacity failur\\r\\ne. Increase/parameterize `allLoginTimeoutMs` beyond ramp/readiness, ensure every login thread can reach the barrier, an\\r\\nd collect target CPU/RSS/GC/EventLoop/connection and JMeter metrics before retrying. Do not begin 3000 until 2000 close\\r\\ns the full protocol and MQ/Outbox gates. [Task 6]\\r\\n- Do not equate MySQL global cumulative `Innodb_row_lock_waits` or `setAutoCommit -> socket read` with this run's row-l\\r\\nock cause: capture `BUSINESS_START/END` deltas and correlate `data_lock_waits`, `data_locks`, and `processlist`. `BUSIN\\r\\nESS_END` and `DRAIN_END` are separate; final queue=0 is not a steady-window pass. [Task 8]\\r\\n- The new `SessionIndexPartitionDispatcher` initially appeared patched but its file was absent -> after adding files, r\\r\\nun `Test-Path`/`Get-Item` before compiling. Its Maven package passed only with `-Dmaven.test.skip=true`; no P1-B load r\\r\\nesult exists. For a targeted reactor test, quote `\\\"-Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false\\\"`; a normal `-DskipTests` bu\\r\\nild was blocked by existing `IMServiceImplTest` missing-method compilation. [Task 8]\\r\\n- Static branch comparison is not a JMeter/service/capacity run. Long Chinese paths can make `git show` fail; prefer sh\\r\\nort paths, `git diff --stat`, class-name search, or the working-tree file. Do not promote virtual users, auth bypasses,\\r\\n or virtual group members into production paths. [Task 9]\\r\\n- Do not treat local synchronous push's lower cmd27 as a throughput gain: first measure its long-lived occupancy of `im\\r\\n-asyncdb-` and the full protocol closure. If high single-host connection tests show duplicate/ACK-pending noise on Java\\r\\n HttpClient `SelectorManager`, distribute load generators and repair the login ramp/barrier before attributing readines\\r\\ns failure to the IM server. [Task 10]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: youpu-cloud-platform / IM message-quote protocol and acceptance design\\r\\nscope: Review and document the server-side message-quote contract, persistence, invalidation, and compatibility rules; \\r\\nthis rollout did not implement business code.\\r\\napplies_to: cwd=D:\\\\workspace\\\\YeQianWorkSpace\\\\youpu\\\\yopu-cloud-platform; reuse_rule=recheck ImCommandConstant, IMHandler\\r\\n, gateway contracts, and the approved document before implementation.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 1: Review and update the message-quote implementation/acceptance plan\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-30T07-11-07-7Fmu-im_message_quote_plan_review_and_protocol_update.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\D:\\\\workspace\\\\\\r\\nYeQianWorkSpace\\\\youpu\\\\yopu-cloud-platform, rollout_path=C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\07\\\\30\\\\rollout-2026-07-30T15\\r\\n-11-07-019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b0b5-901078c5226e.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-30T09:31:48+00:00, thread_id=019fb1dc-d31f-7872-b\\r\\n0b5-901078c5226e, success: design document reviewed and updated)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- content + extra + mentions, extra.replyTo.messageId, /v1/im/message/quote/target, ImCommandConstant, IMHandler, cmd=5\\r\\n, cmd=6, cmd=11, cmd=12, cmd=22, cmd=27, QUOTE_MESSAGE_ID, QUOTE_STATUS, MESSAGE_EXTRA, outbox\\r\\n\\r\\n## User preferences\\r\\n\\r\\n- when the user asked “具体要提供几个接口给客户端” -> state the count of new client APIs, changed existing contracts, c\\r\\nommand matrix, and acceptance evidence directly. [Task 1]\\r\\n- when the user asked “补强后评审” and adopted `content + extra + mentions` -> expose blockers first, then make the use\\r\\nr's protocol the contract and strengthen server validation/state consistency around it. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reusable knowledge\\r\\n\\r\\n- The approved shape is `content + extra + mentions`: client uploads only `extra.replyTo.messageId`; server generates t\\r\\nhe quote snapshot/status/version and returns `extra.replyTo` consistently in ACK, push, and history. `extra` needs vers\\r\\nion, whitelist, and size validation; reject or strip unknown fields. `mentions` remains a separate executable-semantic \\r\\nfield, with no @ business expansion this phase. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Protocol directions: single uplink `cmd=5`, ACK `cmd=6`; group uplink `cmd=11`, ACK/push `cmd=12`; single receive pus\\r\\nh `cmd=27`; revoke/quote invalidation `cmd=22`. String fast paths `handleSingleChat(String)` and `handleGroupChat(Strin\\r\\ng)` must parse nested `extra.replyTo.messageId`; use DTO + `ObjectMapper`, not hand-written JSON. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Add one original-message-location HTTP API, `/v1/im/message/quote/target`; the other four are existing payload-contra\\r\\nct changes, not five new APIs. Gateway `/v1/im/**` injects identity; never trust a client `userId`. Persist indexed `QU\\r\\nOTE_MESSAGE_ID`, `QUOTE_STATUS`, snapshot, and state version rather than scanning `MESSAGE_EXTRA`. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Revoke/cleanup is a separate cmd=22 `event` with `eventId`, `rootMessageId`, `stateVersion`, chunked affected quote I\\r\\nDs, `sequence`, and `lastChunk`; clients process idempotently. Keep hot-store updates atomic; use outbox/compensation f\\r\\nor cold store and ES rather than promising a global transaction. Capability downgrade must cover WebSocket, HTTP histor\\r\\ny/offline pull, and device Push. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- Do not confuse uplink, ACK, receive push, and revoke event; verify `ImCommandConstant.java` and `IMHandler` before wr\\r\\niting the command matrix. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Do not mark all system messages non-quotable: freeze an allowlist by `msgType + content` subtype. Do not call design-\\r\\ndocument `git diff --check` success an implementation, DDL, Maven, or release verification. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: Windows screenshot OCR for model-usage/cost questions\\r\\nscope: Extract model-usage data from a supplied Windows screenshot; use when a Chinese “今天花了多少钱/今日模型用量” re\\r\\nquest provides an image but no account entrypoint. Do not turn ambiguous OCR output into a precise cost claim.\\r\\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\Documents; reuse_rule=WinRT OCR availability and installed packages are machine-specific\\r\\n; the confidence and search-boundary safeguards are reusable.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 1: OCR a dark “今日模型用量” screenshot for DeepSeek cost\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- deepseek, 今日模型用量, OCR, Windows.Media.Ocr, WinRT, PowerShell, TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages, zh-Hans-CN, tes\\r\\nseract, cv2, control-chrome, mcp__node_repl__js, gray>150\\r\\n\\r\\n## User preferences\\r\\n\\r\\n- when the user attaches a dark screenshot and asks “deepseek今天花了多少钱” -> treat the screenshot as the primary dat\\r\\na source; start with local OCR and use a logged-in platform only when available, rather than first asking for an accoun\\r\\nt entrypoint. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Reusable knowledge\\r\\n\\r\\n- This machine has no tesseract/pytesseract/easyocr/paddleocr; Python 3.12 has PIL/cv2/numpy. The dependency-free optio\\r\\nn is `Windows.Media.Ocr` with `zh-Hans-CN`, after loading WinRT type projections and using generic `AsTask`/`Await`. [T\\r\\nask 1]\\r\\n- For a 185x225 dark image, `gray>150` and >4px row gaps separated the table header plus five rows. `control-chrome` ne\\r\\neds `mcp__node_repl__js`; without that tool, a logged-in Chrome fallback is unavailable. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n## Failures and how to do differently\\r\\n\\r\\n- `Unable to find type` and `Cannot index into a null array` mean the WinRT types or generic `AsTask` method were not l\\r\\noaded: call `Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Runtime.WindowsRuntime`, preload the required `[Windows...., ContentType=Win\\r\\ndowsRuntime]` types, and filter reflection with `$_.IsGenericMethod`. Use `TryCreateFromUserProfileLanguages()` instead\\r\\n of an unloaded `Windows.Globalization.Language`. [Task 1]\\r\\n- Small dark-image numerals were inconsistent across OCR/enhancement attempts. If the number drives a cost decision, cr\\r\\noss-check multiple enhancements and manually inspect, or get source/platform data; do not report a single OCR result as\\r\\n exact. Bound any `rg` search to likely app directories and a timeout—recursing through `D:\\\\soft`/AppData was slow and \\r\\nirrelevant. [Task 1]\\r\\n\\r\\n# Task Group: Windows Fiddler Classic and MEmu HTTP/WebSocket capture setup\\r\\nscope: Configure both local MEmu instances for Fiddler Classic HTTP/HTTPS capture, maintain reboot recovery, and distin\\r\\nguish direct IM WebSocket traffic from observed Fiddler frames.\\r\\napplies_to: cwd=C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\Documents; reuse_rule=local executable paths, ADB serials, certificates, UI state, and N\\r\\nAT/host routing are machine/session-specific; do not call WebSocket capture complete without a fresh `101 Switching Pro\\r\\ntocols` session and frames.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 1: Configure Fiddler Classic and MEmu proxy/HTTPS capture\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\D\\r\\nocuments, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\07\\\\29\\\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9eb\\r\\ne-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: Fi\\r\\nddler Classic on 8866 and both VM HTTP/HTTPS proxy paths verified)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- Fiddler Classic, Fiddler Everywhere, MEmu, adb.exe, memuc.exe, 127.0.0.1:21503, 127.0.0.1:21513, 10.0.2.2:8866, 26995\\r\\n3fb.0, AllowRemote, CaptureCONNECT\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 2: Use a narrow host allowlist and reversible proxy on/off workflow\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_android_proxy_cert_capture_setup.md (cwd=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\D\\r\\nocuments, rollout_path=\\\\\\\\?\\\\C:\\\\Users\\\\79873\\\\.codex\\\\sessions\\\\2026\\\\07\\\\29\\\\rollout-2026-07-29T09-44-35-019fab8b-84a0-7430-9eb\\r\\ne-eda54efd9ea5.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-27T02:28:51+00:00, thread_id=019fab8b-84a0-7430-9ebe-eda54efd9ea5, success: Cu\\r\\nstomRules allowlist and direct-connect recovery verified)\\r\\n\\r\\n### keywords\\r\\n\\r\\n- CustomRules.js, OnBeforeRequest, ui-hide, youpu, youpucq, youpuzg, 10.168.1.232, 10.168.1.233, settings delete global\\r\\n http_proxy, direct 200, Live Traffic, Inspectors, WebSocket, Messages\\r\\n\\r\\n## Task 3: Diagnose direct IM WebSocket bypass and restore HTTPS capture after emulator reboot\\r\\n\\r\\n### rollout_summary_files\\r\\n\\r\\n- rollout_summaries/2026-07-29T01-44-35-GAwl-fiddler_memu_a